{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CytXRijAkc9eHvZk7YwAWC","type":"tool_result","content":"290\t\n291\t**Op 4, Sticks and Stones (Bone Mend).** Sabine's cold commentary replaces some of Reyes's lines.\n292\t\n293\t1. Open, then Drain.\n294\t2. Bone Mend: grab six fragments (two under pools), rotate while held (right stick, mouse wheel or Q/E), and release onto the bone's silhouette. It snaps within ±15°; within ±5° is CLEAN.\n295\t3. Gel cement along the seams.\n296\t4. An artery pops: a sudden bleeder to Suture fast.\n297\t5. Scripted **Code Blue** teaches paddles.\n298\t6. Suture, Gel, Dressing. Sabine: \"Adequate.\"\n299\t\n300\t**Op 5, Introit** (section 6). Scanner reveals something moving, then the fight. Afterwards Laser six eggs, Suture, Gel, Dressing.\n301\t\n302\t**Op 6, Cold Hands (transplant, as Sabine).** The player has The Second Look.\n303\t\n304\t1. Open.\n305\t2. Forceps place clamps on two vessels.\n306\t3. Short Scalpel strokes cut them.\n307\t4. Forceps lift out the failing kidney.\n308\t5. Fetch the donor kidney from the ice tray. A separate **cold-time bar** (120 s) starts.\n309\t6. Suture three anastomoses (artery, vein, ureter): precise, short.\n310\t7. Unclamp in the right order. The first time, a hidden clot bursts regardless; Sabine: \"Again.\" This forces a prompt to use the Second Look.\n311\t8. The kidney pinks up as blood returns, the game's most satisfying visual payoff. Tween its ramp from grey-plum to warm red.\n312\t9. A scan shows dormant Mercy in the removed-donor-tissue sample: story hook. Close.\n313\t\n314\t**Op 7, Lacrimosa** and **Op 8, Dies Irae** (section 6). Each has a short exploratory opening and a close.\n315\t\n316\t**Op 9, Libera Me** (section 6). The comm strip shows `NO SIGNAL`. There is no hint marker, no voice. A bot-driven partner hand shares the table.\n317\t\n318\t**Op 10, Do No Harm.** No time pressure in spirit: generous clock, soft music, no attacks. A pale strain lies curled along her spine and does not fight.\n319\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"75cb47e1-b6a0-4fd4-af20-38b42f9600a5","uuid":"a90ca9cd-201f-4607-afce-bd8479257836","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:20:36.262Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-162024__x24ebb3/work/PLAN.md","content":"\n**Op 4, Sticks and Stones (Bone Mend).** Sabine's cold commentary replaces some of Reyes's lines.\n\n1. Open, then Drain.\n2. Bone Mend: grab six fragments (two under pools), rotate while held (right stick, mouse wheel or Q/E), and release onto the bone's silhouette. It snaps within ±15°; within ±5° is CLEAN.\n3. Gel cement along the seams.\n4. An artery pops: a sudden bleeder to Suture fast.\n5. Scripted **Code Blue** teaches paddles.\n6. Suture, Gel, Dressing. Sabine: \"Adequate.\"\n\n**Op 5, Introit** (section 6). Scanner reveals something moving, then the fight. Afterwards Laser six eggs, Suture, Gel, Dressing.\n\n**Op 6, Cold Hands (transplant, as Sabine).** The player has The Second Look.\n\n1. Open.\n2. Forceps place clamps on two vessels.\n3. Short Scalpel strokes cut them.\n4. Forceps lift out the failing kidney.\n5. Fetch the donor kidney from the ice tray. A separate **cold-time bar** (120 s) starts.\n6. Suture three anastomoses (artery, vein, ureter): precise, short.\n7. Unclamp in the right order. The first time, a hidden clot bursts regardless; Sabine: \"Again.\" This forces a prompt to use the Second Look.\n8. The kidney pinks up as blood returns, the game's most satisfying visual payoff. Tween its ramp from grey-plum to warm red.\n9. A scan shows dormant Mercy in the removed-donor-tissue sample: story hook. Close.\n\n**Op 7, Lacrimosa** and **Op 8, Dies Irae** (section 6). Each has a short exploratory opening and a close.\n\n**Op 9, Libera Me** (section 6). The comm strip shows `NO SIGNAL`. There is no hint marker, no voice. A bot-driven partner hand shares the table.\n\n**Op 10, Do No Harm.** No time pressure in spirit: generous clock, soft music, no attacks. A pale strain lies curled along her spine and does not fight.\n","numLines":30,"startLine":290,"totalLines":894}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01CytXRijAkc9eHvZk7YwAWC","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgkdze3VpgPMaVru7X72M","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015UjUJaBZiD7RJXsU9A6oyH","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-162024__x24ebb3/work/PLAN.md","offset":380},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9993,"cache_read_input_tokens":28514,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9993},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"75cb47e1-b6a0-4fd4-af20-38b42f9600a5","uuid":"0f5a0482-9896-41c6-8fa1-d5e7653371ca","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:20:36.363Z","request_id":"req_011CgkdzdocLhPUMrZcVTkjt","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_015UjUJaBZiD7RJXsU9A6oyH":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-162024__x24ebb3/work/PLAN.md","offset":380}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015UjUJaBZiD7RJXsU9A6oyH","type":"tool_result","content":"380\t\n381\t### AI Hub session (protocol v1, client 1.4.0)\n382\t\n383\tFetch `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` from `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/` (✔ public) and read that folder's `README.md`.\n384\t\n385\t✔ A spike with this exact shape passed every run: the real engine in every copy, 2 and 4 players, 150 ± 50 ms, 5% loss, host-leave, server, solo. It was ready in under 2 s on software WebGPU.\n386\t\n387\t```js\n388\tif (window.AIHub?.active) {\n389\t  const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\n390\t  if (info) return runSession(info);       // null: no hub after all, fall through to the normal game\n391\t}\n392\trunStandalone();\n393\t\n394\tfunction runSession(info) {\n395\t  AIHub.on('card', updateCard);            // { left, paused, starting, ready, asked, ... }\n396\t  AIHub.on('start', beginCountdown);       // play begins when AIHub.time() >= 0\n397\t  AIHub.on('message', onMessage);\n398\t  AIHub.on('leave', ({ id }) => retireSeat(id));\n399\t  AIHub.on('time-up', () => { if (AIHub.isHost) finishRound(false); });\n400\t  AIHub.on('end', stopInputAndSound);      // playMusic(null), stopLoops(), nothing more sent\n401\t  startHostLoopIfHost();                   // on a timer from AIHub.time(), never from the renderer\n402\t  if (info.server) { AIHub.ready(); return; }   // ✔ a server copy never starts the engine\n403\t  startEngineThen(() => AIHub.ready());    // no key press\n404\t}\n405\t```\n406\t\n407\t- **No WebGPU in a session:** `AIHub.fail('WebGPU unavailable')`. Check `navigator.gpu` before `Engine.start` and show a friendly message outside a session.\n408\t- **Session rules:** no title, menus, pause, saves, attract or dev mode. Options does nothing. No alert/confirm/prompt, no new tabs, no sockets, no chat. Names come only from `info.players` and are drawn with `hud.text`. Don't use `Math.random` for gameplay; seed the sim with `AIHub.rng('deal')`.\n409\t- **The card (CardStage):** OR-7 wide shot with one masked figure per player in their seat colour, title, players with READY marks, how to win, controls for this player's device, time left. Answers:\n410\t  - Enter, ✕ or a tap on Ready: `AIHub.answer('ready')`.\n411\t  - △, M or a tap on More Time: `AIHub.answer('more')`.\n412\t  - ✔ `ctx.input.wasPressed('Enter')` catches the harness's synthetic key.\n413\t- **Round choice:** `info.round` cycles the session list: Pile-Up, then trimmed Introit, Lacrimosa and Dies Irae fights (`session: true` stages, ≤ 4 minutes). All tools unlocked, hints on, Reyes's lines on.\n414\t- **Finish:** when the patient is saved or lost, or at `time-up`:\n415\t  ```js\n416\t  AIHub.finish({ standings: groupsByPoints, scores, won: patientSaved, stats, awards });\n417\t  ```\n418\t  - Every present player must appear once in `standings`.\n419\t  - Limits: 6 stats per player (name and text ≤ 16 chars), 3 awards per player (title ≤ 24, detail ≤ 40).\n420\t  - Awards: STEADIEST HAND, MOST STITCHES, SAVED THE DAY, SLOPPIEST (kindly).\n421\t\n422\t### Networking\n423\t\n424\t- **Authority:** the host's copy runs the sim on a timer (`setInterval`, catch-up from `AIHub.time()`). A hidden tab must not stall it, and a server copy has no renderer.\n425\t- **Clients to host:** 15 Hz `AIHub.send({t:'i', n, x, z, tool, use, gift, steady}, { to: AIHub.host, reliable: false })`, always sent, even idle (the harness requires traffic both ways).\n426\t- **Host to all:** 12 Hz unreliable snapshot, plus 1 Hz reliable keyframe, plus up to 4 Hz reliable event batches (ratings, comm lines, stage changes, sounds).\n427\t  - That totals at most 17 messages/s against the limit of 20/s (burst 40). Add your own token bucket; the client drops over-limit sends.\n428\t- **Sizes:** keep unreliable snapshots ≤ 1,100 bytes (above about 1,200 they fragment and are lost whole). Use fixed-point ints in positional arrays: `[id, kind, x, z, a, b]`. Gel masks are a coarse bitset. Keyframes ≤ 16 KB. Test both at each op's peak.\n429\t- **Feel:** a client moves its own tip locally at once using the same integrator and corrects gently if it drifts over 1 unit. It plays tool loops, sparks and rumble locally. Everything else renders from interpolated snapshots about 120 ms behind. The view reads a plain state object, whether from a local sim or the network.\n430\t\n431\t**Head tags** (session client first, unmodified, see section 14):\n432\t- `hub:session` 1\n433\t- `hub:session-players` 1-4\n434\t- `hub:session-mode` shared-world\n435\t- `hub:session-minutes` 4\n436\t- `hub:webgpu` required\n437\t- `hub:session-goal` \"Keep the patient alive and top the team score\" (≤ 60 chars)\n438\t- `hub:session-howto` \"Stick/mouse: move tool. R2/click: use. Right stick/1-8: pick tool.\" (≤ 80 chars)\n439\t\n440\t---\n441\t\n442\t## 8. Screens and flow\n443\t\n444\t**10-foot rules** for every screen:\n445\t\n446\t- One idea per screen; at most about 8 rows at once.\n447\t- Text never below the engine font at scale 1 (at 1080p that is 28-pixel caps, ✔ reads well). Headers at scale 2+.\n448\t- A big focused item with a bright marker. Clipboard, chart and rubber-stamp motifs, never tables of data.\n449\t- Everything lives on the HUD canvas (`ctx.hud`), anchored to `hud.width`/`hud.height`, which vary (section 9). `hud.text` doesn't wrap and clips at the edge ✔, so write a `wrap(text, width)` helper using `hud.measure`.\n450\t- The font auto-uppercases and has `. , : ; ! ? - + % / ( ) [ ] ' \" # & * = < >` ✔. Anything else, em dashes and ellipsis characters included, draws as a gap: type `-` and `...`.\n451\t\n452\t**Flow**\n453\t\n454\tTitle → Main → Story scene → Briefing → Operation → Results → next. Save after every op.\n455\t\n456\t- **Title:** dim OR-7, swinging lamp, title drawn big with an EKG line through it. \"Press ✕\" or \"Press Enter/Click\", following the last input. Theme music. Any input leads to Main.\n457\t- **Main menu** (over the dim theatre, the camera drifting):\n458\t  - **ON CALL:** Continue or New Shift, then pick a difficulty.\n459\t  - **OPERATING LOG:** replay cleared ops, showing best rank and a patient line. One chart at a time, flip with ←/→.\n460\t  - **CONSULT**\n461\t  - **SETTINGS**\n462\t  - **ABOUT**\n463\t- **Story scene:** set plus busts. ✕/Enter/click advances; hold △/Esc to skip. Typewriter text with gibberish voice, the speaker leaning in and the other dimmed. Occasional wide shots use full-body figures and the engine's `Timeline`.\n464\t- **Briefing:** a clipboard chart: patient name, age, job, hook, the op's title stamped, and the one-line objective. Not a stats page. Then the camera dives from the OR-7 wide shot down onto the field (fly the three.js camera directly) with an iris transition.\n465\t- **Operation HUD** (art pixels at 270 height):\n466\t  - **Top strip, 20 tall:** VITALS number at scale 2 and a live EKG on the left, clock at centre, Composure at right.\n467\t  - **Bottom strip, 32 tall:** speaker name and up to two lines of comm text.\n468\t  - **Bottom-right:** the tool wheel (about 48 square), with the current tool in the centre, clickable.\n469\t  - **Dose count** by the wheel. **Rating pop-ups** at scale 2 near the tip.\n470\t  - **Comm bust:** a tiny real 3D bust of the speaker placed near the camera at the top-left corner, with `castShadow = false`, so in-op talk uses the same models and mouth animation.\n471\t- **Results:** the chart drops in. Lines tally one at a time with ticks: time, vitals, technique, streak, mistakes. Rank stamp slams with shake, then a Reyes comment, then the patient's follow-up line for that rank.\n472\t- **Pause (Options/Esc):** Resume, Retry Stage, Restart, Settings, **Dev Mode**, Quit to Menu. Use your own pause flag and stop stepping the sim. ✔ Don't use `engine.paused`: `update()` stops running and your menu dies. Disabled in a session.\n473\t- **Settings** (own HUD screen, navigable by pad):\n474\t  - Music (**10% default**), Sound, Voices.\n475\t  - Button glyphs (PlayStation/Xbox), Aim Assist, Cursor Speed, Rumble, Gift Hold/Toggle.\n476\t  - Look (engine looks), Pixel Size, Screen Shake, Reduce Flashes, Text Speed, Difficulty, Fullscreen, Reset.\n477\t- **About/Credits:** paged, big text. Pages: Source Information; Testing Feedback; Engine Feedback; Prompt Feedback; Credits. All field labels and answers as your brief lists them. Data in `src/content/about.js`, filled in last. Credits condense the kit's `CREDITS.md` (engine MIT, three.js, Rapier, Kenney furniture CC0) and the game's own \"all art and audio written in code\".\n478\t\n479\t**Touch-only devices.** Detect before `Engine.start`: no `(any-pointer: fine)`, `maxTouchPoints > 0`, no gamepad. ✔ Phones report art like 136×276 at 8×, so the HUD would be a narrow column.\n480\t\n481\t- Show a DOM overlay with the exact text `Controller or keyboard required`, plus the engine's ⚙: ✔ `settings: { button: 'top-right' }` shows it on a phone profile and a tap opens the DOM panel.\n482\t- `touch: false` always: ✔ no joystick appears.\n483\t- The attract mode loops behind the message.\n484\t- If a key is pressed or a pad connects, drop the gate and play normally.\n485\t\n486\t**Attract mode.** 10 s with no input on Title or any menu screen starts it. Input means a key, click, mouse move, stick beyond deadzone, pad button or touch; each resets the timer.\n487\t\n488\t- A looping reel of real sim segments of 20 to 30 s each, played by the bot with cheats (god vitals, free Composure): a talking-head snippet, Op 1 hooks, Op 2 scan and laser, Op 3 table swaps, Bone Mend, Introit with The Quiet, Second Look rewind, Lacrimosa, Dies Irae with Code Blue, then Pile-Up with four hands.\n489\t- Banner `DEMO - PRESS ANY BUTTON`. Any input exits at once to Title and is swallowed.\n490\t- It must never touch saves or settings.\n491\t\n492\t**Dev Mode** (from Pause; tabs on L1/R1, Q/E or click):\n493\t\n494\t- **BALANCE:** live sliders, Reset to Defaults (list in section 12).\n495\t- **CHEATS:** God Vitals, Infinite Composure, Freeze Clock, Unlimited Mistakes, Unlock All.\n496\t- **JUMP:** any op and stage, any story scene.\n497\t- **ACTIONS:** Complete Stage, Win Op, Fail Op, Trigger Code Blue, Spawn (pool, bleeder, laceration, hook, strain), Copy Op JSON to console.\n498\t- **VIEW:** hitbox overlay (entity circles and ids), Bot Plays (with skill slider), Sim Speed 0.1× to 3×, Frame Step, FPS and sim stats.\n499\t\n500\t---\n501\t\n502\t## 9. Art direction: what works\n503\t\n504\tThe engine's native style is low-poly 3D turned into pixel art. My mock of the heart arena with this recipe looked like a shipped game. Keep to these numbers unless you can beat them.\n505\t\n506\t**Framing.** `aspect: 'fill'` always. ✔ It gives no black bars:\n507\t\n508\t| Viewport | Art resolution | Scale |\n509\t|---|---|---|\n510\t| 1920×1080 | 480×270 | ×4 |\n511\t| 3840×2160 | 480×270 | ×8 |\n512\t| 1280×720 | 427×240 | ×3 |\n513\t| 1024×768 | 342×256 | ×3 |\n514\t| 800×600 | 400×300 | ×2 |\n515\t| 600×400 | 600×400 | ×1 |\n516\t\n517\tWithout it, 1280×720 letterboxes to 960×540. Lay out all HUD from anchors.\n518\t\n519\t**The look** (✔ crisp outlines on tools and creatures, none on tissue):\n520\t```js\n521\tconst LOOK = (sat = 1, vig = .3, spread = 0) => ({\n522\t  scene: [{ id: 'vignette', params: { intensity: vig } }, { id: 'adjust', params: { saturation: sat, contrast: 1 } }, { id: 'chromatic', params: { spread } }],\n523\t  actors: { pixel: { size: 1, outline: .85, crease: .2 }, filters: [] },\n524\t  environment: { pixel: { size: 1, outline: 0, crease: 0 }, filters: [] },\n525\t});\n526\t```\n527\tThe split look renders two passes (about a third of the frame rate on software WebGPU here). That's fine: your brief puts performance out of scope. `sixteen_bit` dithers the whole frame and hurts readability ✔. Tag every tool, hand, strain and character with `setLookLayer(obj, 'actors')`.\n528\t\n529\t**Camera in surgery:** `{ preset: 'fixed', position: [0, 9.6, 3.1], target: [0, 0, 0.1], fov: 44, minZoom: 1, maxZoom: 1 }`.\n530\t\n531\t- ✔ Without the min/max lock the mouse wheel zooms the \"fixed\" camera, and wheel is our tool cycle.\n532\t- ✔ Enter and WASD don't disturb a fixed rig.\n533\t- ✔ Move the camera for parallax, dives and whip-pans by setting `ctx.camera.camera.position` and `.lookAt()` each frame; it sticks and `rayAt` follows. Add ±0.25 units of drift toward the tip.\n534\t- For narrow windows multiply the camera's distance by `max(1, (16/9) / aspect)`.\n535\t\n536\t**Lighting.**\n537\t\n538\t- Field ✔: sun intensity 1.0 from `[.25, 1, .35]`, ambient 0.55 warm white (`0xfff0e0`), one point light at `[0, 5.2, .4]`, intensity 5, radius 15. Much more than that washes the tissue out.\n539\t- OR-7 wide ✔: sun 0.35, ambient 0.28 cool (`0x8fa8c8`), lamp point light over the table at intensity 14, radius 7, a monitor glow. A dark room with a pool of light is the mood.\n540\t- Never `new PointLight`; use `ctx.lights`.\n541\t\n542\t**The tissue canvas** is the game's signature. Each table has a 480×270 RGBA `DataTexture` on a 192×108 `PlaneGeometry` in `toonMaterial(PALETTE.white, { map })` with `receiveShadow`.\n543\t\n544\t- ✔ Copying the base into the buffer and painting 60 blood discs measured about 0.5 ms a frame.\n545\t- Mapping ✔: `px = (x / 16 + .5) · W`, `py = (z / 9 + .5) · H`, and **flip the plane's UV v** (`uv.setY(i, 1 - uv.getY(i))`), or the paint lands mirrored.\n546\t- Set `magFilter`/`minFilter` Nearest and `needsUpdate` after each paint.\n547\t- Each frame: write the prebuilt base into the buffer, then paint scars, pools, wounds, stitches, gel and burns from sim state. Displace the mesh by `heightAt` plus heartbeat, breathing and bulges, then `computeVertexNormals()`.\n548\t\n549\tBase painting recipe (✔ the look, shown for the heart; each arena has its own ramp and shape):\n550\t```js\n551\tconst BAYER = [0,8,2,10,12,4,14,6,3,11,1,9,15,7,13,5];\n552\tconst RAMP = [0x3c0d24, 0x5e1430, 0x8a1f38, 0xb5343f, 0xd65c4f];      // dark to light, 5 steps\n553\t// per texel: m = shape mask (0 outside the organ); light = 0.25 + 0.75*m + (fbm(x*.9, z*.9) - .5)*.9 + tilt;\n554\t// index = floor(clamp(light)*5 + BAYER[(px&3) + (py&3)*4]/16*.9 - .2) into RAMP (ordered dither between bands)\n555\t// outside the organ: a dark cavity colour (0x1c0a18) with noise blotches of RAMP[0]\n556\t// then: fat blobs (0xe9c46a) where fbm(x*1.6, z*2.4) > .66 near edges\n557\t//       vessels: random-walk branches (heading += noise*.55, step .09, width 2 then 1, branch at 4.5%), arteries 0xf08a5d, veins 0x2e1a52\n558\t//       wet sheen: a few hundred single 0xf6d0c0 texels on the light-facing side\n559\t```\n560\t\n561\t| Arena | Ramp feel, shape |\n562\t|---|---|\n563\t| forearm | tan skin ramp, hair flecks, teal drape window |\n564\t| stomach | pink-salmon, folded rugae lines |\n565\t| 3 tables | one skin ramp each, small windows |\n566\t| bone | dark muscle with a white bone silhouette |\n567\t| liver | deep maroon, two big lobes |\n568\t| kidney bed | fat-yellow bed, kidney bean mesh (plum to red tween) |\n569\t| lung | grey-pink, dotted alveoli, breathing |\n570\t| heart | the recipe above |\n571\t| whole chest | ribs, lung and heart together |\n572\t| spine | pale ivory and cool shadow |\n573\t\n574\tFrame every arena with raised teal drapes (boxes, `y` 0.4), steel clamps and retractors. Pools, blood and wounds use 2 or 3 flat colours with animated sparkle texels, plus particles for droplets, smoke and foam (`ctx.particles.register`; sizes are whole art pixels).\n575\t\n576\t**The hand and instruments.** Each is `model()` data with the tip at the origin, pointing −Z. A gloved hand plus forearm from below the frame sells first-person presence, and its cast shadow gives depth ✔.\n577\t\n578\t```js\n579\texport const handDef = model({ id:'glove-hand', about:'Gloved surgeon hand gripping a shaft, wrist toward +Z', tags:['character','hand'], floats:true,\n580\t  palette:{ glove:'sky', fold:'blue', sleeve:'teal' }, parts:[\n581\t  { name:'palm', box:[.72,.3,.8], at:[0,0,0], c:'glove' }, { name:'knuck', box:[.74,.16,.14], at:[0,.12,-.34], c:'fold' },\n582\t  ...[-.27,-.09,.09,.27].flatMap((x,i)=>[{ name:`f${i}a`, box:[.16,.16,.34], at:[x,.05,-.56], rot:[18,0,0], c:'glove' },{ name:`f${i}b`, box:[.15,.15,.26], at:[x,-.09,-.76], rot:[58,0,0], c:'glove' }]),\n583\t  { name:'thumb', box:[.18,.18,.5], at:[-.44,-.04,-.26], rot:[10,-28,0], c:'glove' },\n584\t  { name:'cuff', cyl:[.62,.62,.3], at:[0,0,.54], rot:[90,0,0], c:'fold' }, { name:'wrist', cyl:[.56,1.6,.56], at:[0,0,1.46], rot:[90,0,0], c:'glove' },\n585\t  { name:'sleeve', cyl:[.8,2.6,.8], at:[0,0,3.4], rot:[90,0,0], c:'sleeve' } ]});\n586\t```\n587\t\n588\t- ✔ Placement that read well: tool at `(x, surface + .05, z)`, rotation `(-.5, -.7, 0)`; hand at `tip + (.88, 1.1, 1.25)`, rotation `(-.46, -.72, .2)`.\n589\t- Seats 2 to 4 enter from other corners. Glove colour follows the seat: palette `red`, `blue`, `green`, `sand` in 3D; `info.players[i].color` exactly on the HUD (`hud.text` colours take numbers).\n590\t- Give each tool a distinct silhouette: forceps with moving jaws, curved needle plus thread (try `RopeMesh` with `ropeLine`, and check it reads), drain wand, syringe with moving plunger, laser pen, scanner disc (`hologramMaterial`), gel bottle.\n591\t\n592\t**Busts: the anime talking head.** Build the face and hair from `slab` outlines. ✔ This gives a real anime silhouette in the engine's style at about 150 art pixels tall. Put the head in a named pivot, and the mouth, brows and lids in their own pivots.\n593\t\n594\t```js\n595\tconst FACE = [[-.46,.5],[.46,.5],[.5,.05],[.42,-.28],[.2,-.56],[0,-.68],[-.2,-.56],[-.42,-.28],[-.5,.05]];\n596\tconst FRINGE = [[-.56,.42],[-.6,0],[-.44,.16],[-.4,-.08],[-.22,.24],[-.06,.02],[.06,.26],[.24,.04],[.34,.26],[.46,-.1],[.6,.02],[.56,.42],[.34,.66],[0,.74],[-.34,.66]];\n597\t// parts (head group at [0,1.62,0], pivot:true, name:'head'):\n598\t// { name:'skull', box:[.9,.92,.72], at:[0,.1,-.12] }, { name:'face', slab:FACE, depth:.26, at:[0,0,.14] },\n599\t// { name:'hairfront', slab:FRINGE, depth:.16, at:[0,.22,.26] }, { name:'hairback', box:[.98,.86,.5], at:[0,.2,-.34] },\n600\t// eyes at z≈.28: white box .22×.16, pupil box .12×.16 at z .30; brow box .28×.05 at y .2, rot z -18 (mirror x); nose box; mouth in a pivot group\n601\t```\n602\t\n603\t- ✔ Set `receiveShadow = castShadow = false` on bust meshes or shadow acne scatters triangles over the face.\n604\t- Camera for a close-up ✔: `position [.2, 1.75, 5.1]`, `target [0, 1.42, 0]`, `fov 30`.\n605\t- ✔ A half-`ball` fills its box, so its base sits at `at.y − h/2`: the first cap I built covered the eyes.\n606\t- Emotions are a small pose table per character: neutral, stern, shock, sad, smile, angry, panic (brow rotation and height, lid scale, mouth scale, head tilt). Add a few toggled extras: sweat drop, blush, tear, glasses glint.\n607\t- Mouth scale follows voice syllables, blinks every 2 to 5 s, slight idle sway.\n608\t- Draw big white reaction marks and speed-line flourishes on the HUD for comic beats.\n609\t\n610\t**Full-body figures for wide shots.** ⚠ The bundled hero is a red-capped, moustached plumber in overalls: **do not show `HERO_MODEL`.** But ✔ a `model()` whose pivots carry the hero rig's joint names plays every `HERO_CLIPS` clip through `compileClips(HERO_CLIPS, HERO_RIG, build.object)` and a three.js `AnimationMixer`. I tested Idle, Walk, Wave, Sit and Shout; there are also Victory, Hurt, HitReact, Death, LieIdle, Grab, Triumph and more. The figure faces +Z; its right is −X.\n611\t\n612\t```js\n613\tconst arm=(s,x)=>({ group:[{ name:`upper${s}`, box:[.11,.25,.11], at:[0,-.12,0], c:'scrub' },\n614\t  { group:[{ name:`fore${s}`, box:[.1,.23,.1], at:[0,-.11,0], c:'skin' },\n615\t    { group:[{ name:`glove${s}`, box:[.12,.13,.12], at:[0,-.06,0], c:'glove' }], at:[0,-.23,0], name:`Hand${s}`, pivot:true }], at:[0,-.25,0], name:`Forearm${s}`, pivot:true }],\n616\t  at:[x,.36,0], name:`Arm${s}`, pivot:true });\n617\tconst leg=(s,x)=>({ group:[{ name:`thigh${s}`, box:[.15,.3,.15], at:[0,-.15,0], c:'scrub' },\n618\t  { group:[{ name:`shin${s}`, box:[.13,.22,.13], at:[0,-.11,0], c:'scrub' },\n619\t    { group:[{ name:`shoe${s}`, box:[.15,.1,.28], at:[0,-.05,.06], c:'shoe' }], at:[0,-.22,0], name:`Foot${s}`, pivot:true }], at:[0,-.3,0], name:`Shin${s}`, pivot:true }],\n620\t  at:[x,0,0], name:`Leg${s}`, pivot:true });\n621\t// parts: [{ group:[ { name:'hips', box:[.36,.18,.22], at:[0,.02,0], c:'scrub' },\n622\t//   { group:[ { name:'chest', box:[.38,.42,.24], at:[0,.22,0], c:'scrub' },\n623\t//     { group:[ skull, cap, mask, eyes ], at:[0,.44,0], name:'Head', pivot:true }, arm('R',-.25), arm('L',.25) ], at:[0,.1,0], name:'Torso', pivot:true },\n624\t//   leg('R',-.14), leg('L',.14) ], at:[0,.62,0], name:'Pelvis', pivot:true }]\n625\t```\n626\tVary cap, hair, coat and height per character. Masked surgeons read very well at distance ✔.\n627\t\n628\t**Sets** (each a `model()`/mesh group with a lighting recipe): OR-7 (table, patient under drape, lamp arm, monitor on a stand, instrument tray, gallery glass, doors), scrub room (sinks), Chief's office (desk, window with `Precipitation` rain and harbour lights), ward (beds, `clothGrid` curtains), corridor, Foundation atrium (white, gold, flowers), helipad roof at night in the rain.\n629\t\n630\t- **Generic props** come from the `kenney-furniture` pack (beds, sinks, desks, chairs, cabinets, screens, lamps; search `LIBRARY.md`). Recolour them to steel and hospital tones with `buildModel(id, { catalog: kit, palette: {...} })`; they arrive bright yellow-wood ✔.\n631\t- ✔ **Packs in one file:** put `window.__PIXEL_ASSETS__ = { 'packs/kenney-furniture.json': 'data:application/json;base64,…' }` in a classic script before the module, and `await loadPack('packs/kenney-furniture.json')` works from `file://`.\n632\t- Nice touches if cheap: a `RenderView` live monitor in OR-7, a `Mirror` in the scrub room.\n633\t\n634\t**Check your models.** `node check.mjs --sheets src/content/models/index.js` ✔ draws every def and warns about z-fighting and floating parts. Models need `about` and `tags`; busts and tools need `floats: true`.\n635\t\n636\t**Game feel.** `engine.hitstop`, `engine.shake.add`, `engine.screen.flash/shockwave/cover/reveal`, `Squash` on grabs and hits, rating pop-ups, stamp slams, lamp flicker at low vitals. Honour the Screen Shake and Reduce Flashes settings.\n637\t\n638\t---\n639\t\n640\t## 10. Audio: everything written in code\n641\t\n642\t**Music is 10% by default.** ✔ The engine's default is 0.6, stored in `localStorage['pixel-engine:audio']`. On boot: if that key is absent, call `audio.setVolume('music', 0.1)`, which also stores it. A test asserts this on a fresh profile.\n643\t\n644\t**Voices: Animalese/Simlish gibberish.**\n645\t\n646\t- Pre-render syllables in pure JS at boot: a glottal pulse through two or three formants (`src/audio/voice.js`, testable in Node). Use 3 timbres × 5 vowels × 3 consonant onsets, about 120 ms each.\n647\t- ✔ Wrap the PCM in a WAV header, make a base64 data URL and call `await ctx.audio.load('syl-a', url)`. Then `ctx.audio.play('syl-a', { pitch, volume, pan })`: it works from `file://`, runs through the engine's buses and respects mute.\n648\t- Letters pick syllables deterministically; punctuation shapes rhythm and pitch (\"!\" up and louder, \"?\" rising, \"...\" slow).\n649\t- Each cast member has `{ timbre, basePitch, speed, range }` per the cast table. Reaction barks in surgery use the same system.\n650\t- The Voices slider scales `volume` per play, since the engine has only master, sfx and music channels.\n651\t\n652\t**Sound effects: `SoundDef` data via `ctx.audio.register`.**\n653\t\n654\t- Tools: drain slurp loop (`audio.loop`, pitch follows force), forceps click, hook pop, dish tink, scalpel slice, suture tick (note scale), knot, laser buzz loop, sizzle, scanner ping, gel fizz loop, syringe draw, inject whoosh.\n655\t- Monitors and crisis: EKG beep (pitch and rate follow vitals), alarm, flatline, defib charge whine, CLEAR thump.\n656\t- UI: move, confirm, back, stamp slam, rating chimes.\n657\t- Gifts: heartbeat and inhale, rewind tape.\n658\t- Strains: one signature sound each, plus the knock itself.\n659\t- Room: rain, harbour horn and ship bells under story scenes.\n660\t\n661\t**Music: engine `Song` data (chiptune sequencer), all original compositions.** Don't quote any source music or any real requiem.\n662\t\n663\t- Title theme: a slow, sad triangle lead with a soft pulse.\n664\t- Ward/lounge: tired light jazz.\n665\t- `or-calm`, `or-tense` and `or-critical`: same key and tempo family so switching at bar lines sounds intentional.\n666\t- Four boss themes with saw \"choir\" pads. Dies Irae's tempo follows the heart: restart with new `bpm` at bar lines every few steps.\n667\t- Op 9's silence, then a swell. Op 10 sparse and gentle. Results fanfare and sad variant. Credits.\n668\t\n669\t`MusicDirector` changes tracks at bar lines from vitals and stage. `loadGame` clears music and loops, so have the director restart on each stage.\n670\t\n671\t---\n672\t\n673\t## 11. Architecture\n674\t\n675\t```\n676\tpixel-engine.js check.mjs GUIDE.md API.md …   the kit, unchanged, as it unzips\n677\tindex.html, game.js          game.js exports createGame() and starts the engine only when `document` exists\n678\tsrc/core/     config.js (defaults + live values), rng.js, save.js, meta.js (title, tagline)\n679\tsrc/sim/      op.js, tools.js, entities.js, strains/*.js, scoring.js, bot.js, codec.js, campaign.js\n680\tsrc/content/  ops/*.js, scenes/*.js, lines.js, cast.js, arenas.js, songs.js, sfx.js, icons.js, about.js, models/*.js\n681\tsrc/view/     field.js, hands.js, strains/*.js, sets.js, bust.js, figure.js, fx.js\n682\tsrc/ui/       hud.js, prompts.js, menu.js, then one file per screen\n683\tsrc/stages/   title.js story.js briefing.js operation.js results.js log.js consult.js card.js attract.js\n684\tsrc/input/    devices.js, cursor.js\n685\tsrc/net/      session.js, host.js, client.js\n686\tsrc/audio/    voice.js, director.js\n687\tvendor/       session.js, harness.html, bridge.js, round.js (from the hub, unmodified)\n688\ttools/build.mjs\n689\ttests/        run.mjs, *.test.mjs, browser/*, balance.mjs\n690\tdocs/AUTHORING.md            how to add an op, scene, strain or character\n691\t```\n692\t\n693\t**The one rule that makes everything else possible: `src/sim` and non-model content import nothing from the engine, the DOM or the clock.** The sim is plain data plus pure functions: `sim = createOp(def, { seed, seats, difficulty, config })`, `step(sim, inputsBySeat)` at 60 Hz, `events = drainEvents(sim)`.\n694\t\n695\t- Input per seat is `{ x, z, tool, use, gift, steady, drop, … }`.\n696\t- Randomness comes from its own seeded generator, never `Math.random`.\n697\t- State must survive `structuredClone`. This one rule gives you:\n698\t  - The Second Look.\n699\t  - Determinism: same seed plus inputs gives the same hash.\n700\t  - Tests in Node in milliseconds.\n701\t  - The bot.\n702\t  - A hub server copy with no renderer.\n703\t  - Network snapshots.\n704\t\n705\t**Stages.** Each screen is a `Game` class, swapped with `engine.loadGame(new XStage(args))` under `engine.screen.cover/reveal`. A persistent `App` singleton holds save, settings, devices, config and the director. Set `status()` meaningfully (`op5 stage=2 vitals=64 t=121 score=3400`) and put test handles in `ready(ctx)` (`window.__GAME__ = { app, sim, goto, config }`). In solo, step the sim from `fixedUpdate`; draw in `update`. Cosmetic randomness comes from `ctx.random.fork('fx')`.\n706\t\n707\t**Content is data**, so the rest of the game can be built with ordinary tools (JSON-safe, hot-editable):\n708\t\n709\t```js\n710\texport default { id:'op1', title:'ELEVEN HOOKS', arena:'forearm', surgeon:'ilya', gifts:[], tools:['drain','forceps','suture','gel','syringe'],\n711\t  patient:{ name:'TOMASZ DOLAN', age:52, job:'TRAWLER DECKHAND', hook:\"HIS DAUGHTER'S WEDDING IS SATURDAY.\",\n712\t            followUp:{ S:'He walked her down the aisle. Dry eyes.', C:'He danced badly. She cried anyway.' } },\n713\t  time:240, vitals:{ start:85, drain:.10 }, doses:3, music:'or-calm', par:4200,\n714\t  stages:[\n715\t    { id:'pools', say:'reyes.drainFirst', hint:'drain',\n716\t      spawn:[{ k:'pool', id:'p1', at:[-3,.6], r:1.6 }, { k:'hook', id:'h1', at:[-3,.9], hiddenBy:'p1', arc:.8, pull:1.2 }],\n717\t      until:{ clear:['pool'] },\n718\t      on:{ vitalsBelow:{ 50:{ say:'reyes.stabilize', unlock:'syringe' } } } },\n719\t    …\n720\t  ] };\n721\t```\n722\t\n723\t- Entity kinds (`pool, hook, nick, laceration, incision, tumor, polyp, prop, magnet, bleeder, clamp, vessel, fragment, organ, mask, strain:*`) register their tool handlers in `entities.js`.\n724\t- `until` takes `clear`, `flag`, `all` or `time`. Commands: `say, spawn, remove, unlock, setDrain, music, camera, flag, codeBlue`.\n725\t- Scenes are data too: `{ id, set, music, beats:[{ who, emo, say, cam, cue }] }`. Reaction pools live in `lines.js` (`reyes.mistake[]`, `reyes.clean[]`, `reyes.lowVitals[]`).\n726\t\n727\t**The bot** (`src/sim/bot.js`) reads sim state and produces seat input, with `skill` 0 to 1 scaling speed, path noise, reaction delay and judgement (syringe when low, gifts when useful). It knows a strategy per entity kind. It is one piece of code with four jobs: **attract mode, the whole-game test playthrough, the balance report and the Op 9 partner.** Build it early.\n728\t\n729\t**Engine facts to save you time**\n730\t\n731\t- ✔ `update()` does not run while `engine.paused` is true; it does run at `timeScale = 0`.\n732\t- `loadGame` clears HUD, music, loops, particles and lights; it keeps Input, volumes and look.\n733\t- `engine.settings.open()` is a mouse-driven DOM panel that pauses the engine: use it only on the touch-only path; build your own Settings.\n734\t- Start options: `aspect:'fill'`, `touch:false`, `settings:{ button:false, key: inSession ? false : '<slug>' }`, `background`, plus `withUrlOptions` for review flags.\n735\t- Saves: guarded `localStorage` under a versioned key. In a session the client hands you an empty store.\n736\t- `game.js` must import cleanly in Node for `check.mjs --headless`: guard `document`, `navigator.getGamepads` and `localStorage`.\n737\t- Own URL flags outside a session, for tests: `?op= &stage= &diff= &seed= &bot= &god= &attract= &dev= &scene=`.\n738\t\n739\t---\n740\t\n741\t## 12. Balance\n742\t\n743\t**Dev Mode sliders (live, with Reset to Defaults).** All in `config.js`:\n744\t\n745\t- vitals drain ×, bleed drain, mistake penalty, max mistakes, time limit ×\n746\t- cursor speed, steady factor, aim assist, tool tolerance ×\n747\t- drain rate, laser burn time, syringe dose\n748\t- Composure gain per CLEAN, Quiet slow factor, Quiet drain, Second Look cost and seconds\n749\t- strain speed ×, strain HP ×, Dies Irae base BPM\n750\t- Code Blue zone width, co-op scale per seat\n751\t\n752\t**`node tests/balance.mjs`** runs each op on the bot at skills 0.4, 0.7 and 1.0 and prints time used, final vitals, mistakes and rank. Targets on Resident:\n753\t\n754\t| Bot skill | Should | |\n755\t|---|---|---|\n756\t| 0 (idle, no input) | fail every op | |\n757\t| 0.4 | clear Ops 1 to 3, may lose bosses | a nervous beginner |\n758\t| 0.7 | clear all, mostly B or A, at least 20% clock left outside bosses | a decent player |\n759\t| 1.0 | S on all | sets `par` |\n760\t\n761\t---\n762\t\n763\t## 13. Testing\n764\t\n765\tOne command: `node tests/run.mjs` prints only failures and one count line. An optional filter (`sim`, `content`, `browser`, `hub`) lets you rerun only what you changed.\n766\t\n767\t**Node (fast, most tests):**\n768\t\n769\t- Each tool's rules, success and mistake paths.\n770\t- Every op: idle fails; bot 0.7 clears; determinism hash stable; retry-from-stage works.\n771\t- Code Blue paths, The Quiet's time scale, The Second Look's exact restore.\n772\t- Scoring and rank bounds.\n773\t- Slider apply and reset.\n774\t- Codec round trip and sizes at each op's peak.\n775\t- **Whole-game scripted playthrough:** `campaign.js` driven by the bot through every scene and op to credits, with save and unlock checks.\n776\t\n777\t**Content lint:**\n778\t\n779\t- Cast and sets referenced exist; every tool used; all text fits two wrapped lines at 342 art pixels wide; every character is in the font's set; glyph tokens valid.\n780\t- No `TODO` or placeholder strings; About has every field.\n781\t- No forbidden source names.\n782\t- `check.mjs --sheets` clean of problems.\n783\t\n784\t**Browser (Chromium, one or two at a time):** launch args ✔ `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader --autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required`.\n785\t\n786\tSoftware WebGPU runs at 5 to 30 fps here; prefer the sim's state and `engine.step()` over waiting, and use a 960×540 viewport for logic. A pad stub:\n787\t```js\n788\twindow.__pad = { connected:true, mapping:'standard', index:0, id:'stub', axes:[0,0,0,0], buttons:Array.from({length:17},()=>({pressed:false,value:0})), vibrationActuator:{ playEffect:()=>Promise.resolve('complete') } };\n789\tnavigator.getGamepads = () => [window.__pad, null, null, null];   // add_init_script\n790\t```\n791\tCover:\n792\t\n793\t- The built page from `file://`: boots, no errors. Outside a session `AIHub.active` is false and `AIHub.seeded` is not true. Enter, Space, Enter, Space then still draws (the hub's own \"on its own\" check).\n794\t- Fresh profile: music slider 0.1.\n795\t- Menu navigation by pad stub, keys and mouse (hover moves focus).\n796\t- Prompts switch with the last device; the Xbox option swaps glyphs.\n797\t- A real drain and forceps action by mouse and by pad stub (the sim state changes at the aimed spot).\n798\t- Attract: idle 10 s starts it; key and pad each exit; save untouched.\n799\t- Touch-only with `p.devices['Pixel 7']`: the exact text, the ⚙, no joystick, attract runs.\n800\t- Pause, then Dev Mode: a slider changes live config; reset restores it.\n801\t- Couch co-op with two stub pads: two independent tips.\n802\t- `engine.errors` and `gpuErrors` empty throughout.\n803\t\n804\t**Sound:** render syllables and `SoundDef`s (`renderSound`) in Node: non-silent, finite. In the page, `audio.counts` rise while talking. An `AnalyserNode` level check on one voice line.\n805\t\n806\t**Hub:** copy `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` beside the built page in `dist/`. Serve **`python3 -u -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1`**. ✔ The `-u` matters: when you read the port from a pipe without it, the line never arrives and your script hangs (this cost me about fifteen minutes). Stop that server by its PID. Run these with launch args plus `--no-sandbox`, a 1600×1000 viewport, and wait for `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`:\n807\t```\n808\tharness.html?game=game.html&auto=1&players=2\n809\tharness.html?game=game.html&auto=1&players=3&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5\n810\tharness.html?game=game.html&auto=1&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5\n811\tharness.html?game=game.html&auto=1&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&scenario=host-leave\n812\tharness.html?game=game.html&auto=1&players=2&scenario=server\n813\t```\n814\tAll must give `window.__hubCheck.pass === true`.\n815\t\n816\t**Kit tools** ✔ all work here after `npm install playwright@1.63.0` in the dev folder (about 1 to 3 s each): `node check.mjs` (serves on an OS-picked 127.0.0.1 port), `node check.mjs --headless game.js --keys …`, `node check.mjs --sheets …`.\n817\t\n818\t**Screenshots only for what scripts can't judge**, at 1920×1080: each arena, each set, each bust, title, results, HUD readability. Look at them. Blank WebGPU canvases can happen; ✔ here `page.screenshot` captured every frame fine.\n819\t\n820\t---\n821\t\n822\t## 14. Build and packaging\n823\t\n824\t`tools/build.mjs` ✔ (this exact recipe gave a 6 MB page that booted from `file://` in about 1 s on software WebGPU):\n825\t\n826\t```js\n827\texecFileSync('esbuild', ['game.js','--bundle','--format=esm','--platform=browser','--target=es2022','--outfile=dist/bundle.js']);\n828\tconst js = readFileSync('dist/bundle.js','utf8').replace(/<\\/script/gi,'<\\\\/script');\n829\tconst session = readFileSync('vendor/session.js','utf8');           // verbatim: the hub compares it byte for byte\n830\tconst pack = readFileSync('packs/kenney-furniture.json').toString('base64');\n831\tconst html = `<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n832\t<script>\\n${session}\\n</script>\n833\t<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n834\t<title>${TITLE} — ${TAGLINE}</title> …description, theme-color, data-URL icon, hub:* tags…\n835\t</head><body><div id=\"app\"></div>\n836\t<script>window.__PIXEL_ASSETS__={'packs/kenney-furniture.json':'data:application/json;base64,${pack}'};</script>\n837\t<script type=\"module\">\\n${js}\\n</script></body></html>`;\n838\t```\n839\t\n840\t- The output name comes from your brief: one constant at the top of the script. Write `dist/game.html` for the tests and a copy where your brief wants the deliverable.\n841\t- Don't minify the HTML or touch the session client's text.\n842\t- Also add `hub:type` Game, `hub:source` for the source, and an emblem icon as a data URL.\n843\t- When you report research, say this plan's planner read the source's Wikipedia page, the hub's protocol and the engine kit, and ran engine spikes; add anything you did yourself.\n844\t- For the exit-interview file your brief asks for, `aiHub.genre` is `Simulation`, `players` `1–4`, `series` `Trauma Center`. Good tags: `3d`, `pixel art`, `story`, `co-op`, `boss fights`, `comedy`.\n845\t\n846\t---\n847\t\n848\t## 15. Order of work\n849\t\n850\tBuild in this order. Keep the game running and the tests green after each step.\n851\t\n852\t1. **Skeleton.** Unzip the kit and move the contents of its `pixel-engine/` folder to the dev folder root. `npm install playwright@1.63.0` there. Then: build script, test runner, an empty stage booting from `file://`, music default, input devices with pad stub test.\n853\t2. **One great op.** Sim core, tissue canvas, hand and tools, HUD, Drain, Forceps, Suture, Gel, Syringe, Op 1 playable on pad, mouse and keys. Make this feel wonderful before moving on.\n854\t3. **All tools and the bot.** Scalpel, Laser, Scanner; Ops 2 and 3; Code Blue; The Quiet; bot and balance report; whole-op tests.\n855\t4. **The drama.** Busts, figures, sets, story stage, voices, sound effects, music director, results, saves. Eps 1 to 3 flow end to end.\n856\t5. **The shell.** Title, menus, prompts, settings, pause, Dev Mode, attract, touch gate, About.\n857\t6. **Bosses and the rest.** Second Look, Bone Mend, transplant, Introit, Lacrimosa, Dies Irae, Libera Me, Do No Harm, all scenes, campaign playthrough test.\n858\t7. **Consult.** Couch first (it proves the seats), then session, card, net, harness passes.\n859\t8. **Polish and balance.** Juice, feel, per-arena art, tune against the targets, full screenshot pass at 1080p, `docs/AUTHORING.md`.\n860\t9. **Finish.** Fill in About and your chat reply and exit-interview file as your brief says.\n861\t\n862\t**If you run short, cut whole content rather than leave anything half-made** (the brief forbids stubs). Cut in this order:\n863\t\n864\t1. The `RenderView` and `Mirror` touches.\n865\t2. Extra session fights (keep Pile-Up).\n866\t3. Op 3's third table.\n867\t4. Lacrimosa's crawling phase.\n868\t5. Op 6's cold-time bar.\n869\t\n870\tNever cut: Ops 1, 2, 5, 8, 9; both gifts; Code Blue; attract; Dev Mode; hub conformance; couch co-op.\n871\t\n872\t## 16. Done means\n873\t\n874\t| The brief asks for | Where |\n875\t|---|---|\n876\t| Genre and perspective chosen | §1 |\n877\t| Title by the brief's method | Yours, `src/core/meta.js` |\n878\t| One HTML, engine unmodified, session client verbatim | §14 |\n879\t| Native art plus new assets | §9 |\n880\t| Native animation plus new animations | §6, §9 (`HERO_CLIPS` on custom rigs, procedural tools) |\n881\t| All audio in code, gibberish voices, music at 10% | §10 |\n882\t| AI Hub integration and the game on its own | §7, §13 |\n883\t| Feature-complete demo showing every mechanic | §3, §5, §6 |\n884\t| World, characters, themes, tone, writing style | §2 |\n885\t| Infrastructure for more content with normal tools | §11, `docs/AUTHORING.md`, Dev Mode's Copy Op JSON |\n886\t| Dev mode from pause, live sliders, reset | §8, §12 |\n887\t| Attract after 10 s, any input exits | §8 |\n888\t| Controller-first at 10 feet, native keyboard and mouse, prompts by last input, Xbox option | §4, §8 |\n889\t| No dense data screens | §8 |\n890\t| Touch-only gate, settings button, attract runs | §8 |\n891\t| Tests behind one command, whole-game playthrough | §13 |\n892\t| No TODOs or placeholders | §13 lint |\n893\t| Source Information, Testing, Engine and Prompt Feedback in chat and About; exit interview | §8, §14, your brief |\n894\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"75cb47e1-b6a0-4fd4-af20-38b42f9600a5","uuid":"7573eac5-d3f1-4183-b013-a78747c57dca","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:20:36.515Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-162024__x24ebb3/work/PLAN.md","content":"\n### AI Hub session (protocol v1, client 1.4.0)\n\nFetch `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` from `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/` (✔ public) and read that folder's `README.md`.\n\n✔ A spike with this exact shape passed every run: the real engine in every copy, 2 and 4 players, 150 ± 50 ms, 5% loss, host-leave, server, solo. It was ready in under 2 s on software WebGPU.\n\n```js\nif (window.AIHub?.active) {\n  const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\n  if (info) return runSession(info);       // null: no hub after all, fall through to the normal game\n}\nrunStandalone();\n\nfunction runSession(info) {\n  AIHub.on('card', updateCard);            // { left, paused, starting, ready, asked, ... }\n  AIHub.on('start', beginCountdown);       // play begins when AIHub.time() >= 0\n  AIHub.on('message', onMessage);\n  AIHub.on('leave', ({ id }) => retireSeat(id));\n  AIHub.on('time-up', () => { if (AIHub.isHost) finishRound(false); });\n  AIHub.on('end', stopInputAndSound);      // playMusic(null), stopLoops(), nothing more sent\n  startHostLoopIfHost();                   // on a timer from AIHub.time(), never from the renderer\n  if (info.server) { AIHub.ready(); return; }   // ✔ a server copy never starts the engine\n  startEngineThen(() => AIHub.ready());    // no key press\n}\n```\n\n- **No WebGPU in a session:** `AIHub.fail('WebGPU unavailable')`. Check `navigator.gpu` before `Engine.start` and show a friendly message outside a session.\n- **Session rules:** no title, menus, pause, saves, attract or dev mode. Options does nothing. No alert/confirm/prompt, no new tabs, no sockets, no chat. Names come only from `info.players` and are drawn with `hud.text`. Don't use `Math.random` for gameplay; seed the sim with `AIHub.rng('deal')`.\n- **The card (CardStage):** OR-7 wide shot with one masked figure per player in their seat colour, title, players with READY marks, how to win, controls for this player's device, time left. Answers:\n  - Enter, ✕ or a tap on Ready: `AIHub.answer('ready')`.\n  - △, M or a tap on More Time: `AIHub.answer('more')`.\n  - ✔ `ctx.input.wasPressed('Enter')` catches the harness's synthetic key.\n- **Round choice:** `info.round` cycles the session list: Pile-Up, then trimmed Introit, Lacrimosa and Dies Irae fights (`session: true` stages, ≤ 4 minutes). All tools unlocked, hints on, Reyes's lines on.\n- **Finish:** when the patient is saved or lost, or at `time-up`:\n  ```js\n  AIHub.finish({ standings: groupsByPoints, scores, won: patientSaved, stats, awards });\n  ```\n  - Every present player must appear once in `standings`.\n  - Limits: 6 stats per player (name and text ≤ 16 chars), 3 awards per player (title ≤ 24, detail ≤ 40).\n  - Awards: STEADIEST HAND, MOST STITCHES, SAVED THE DAY, SLOPPIEST (kindly).\n\n### Networking\n\n- **Authority:** the host's copy runs the sim on a timer (`setInterval`, catch-up from `AIHub.time()`). A hidden tab must not stall it, and a server copy has no renderer.\n- **Clients to host:** 15 Hz `AIHub.send({t:'i', n, x, z, tool, use, gift, steady}, { to: AIHub.host, reliable: false })`, always sent, even idle (the harness requires traffic both ways).\n- **Host to all:** 12 Hz unreliable snapshot, plus 1 Hz reliable keyframe, plus up to 4 Hz reliable event batches (ratings, comm lines, stage changes, sounds).\n  - That totals at most 17 messages/s against the limit of 20/s (burst 40). Add your own token bucket; the client drops over-limit sends.\n- **Sizes:** keep unreliable snapshots ≤ 1,100 bytes (above about 1,200 they fragment and are lost whole). Use fixed-point ints in positional arrays: `[id, kind, x, z, a, b]`. Gel masks are a coarse bitset. Keyframes ≤ 16 KB. Test both at each op's peak.\n- **Feel:** a client moves its own tip locally at once using the same integrator and corrects gently if it drifts over 1 unit. It plays tool loops, sparks and rumble locally. Everything else renders from interpolated snapshots about 120 ms behind. The view reads a plain state object, whether from a local sim or the network.\n\n**Head tags** (session client first, unmodified, see section 14):\n- `hub:session` 1\n- `hub:session-players` 1-4\n- `hub:session-mode` shared-world\n- `hub:session-minutes` 4\n- `hub:webgpu` required\n- `hub:session-goal` \"Keep the patient alive and top the team score\" (≤ 60 chars)\n- `hub:session-howto` \"Stick/mouse: move tool. R2/click: use. Right stick/1-8: pick tool.\" (≤ 80 chars)\n\n---\n\n## 8. Screens and flow\n\n**10-foot rules** for every screen:\n\n- One idea per screen; at most about 8 rows at once.\n- Text never below the engine font at scale 1 (at 1080p that is 28-pixel caps, ✔ reads well). Headers at scale 2+.\n- A big focused item with a bright marker. Clipboard, chart and rubber-stamp motifs, never tables of data.\n- Everything lives on the HUD canvas (`ctx.hud`), anchored to `hud.width`/`hud.height`, which vary (section 9). `hud.text` doesn't wrap and clips at the edge ✔, so write a `wrap(text, width)` helper using `hud.measure`.\n- The font auto-uppercases and has `. , : ; ! ? - + % / ( ) [ ] ' \" # & * = < >` ✔. Anything else, em dashes and ellipsis characters included, draws as a gap: type `-` and `...`.\n\n**Flow**\n\nTitle → Main → Story scene → Briefing → Operation → Results → next. Save after every op.\n\n- **Title:** dim OR-7, swinging lamp, title drawn big with an EKG line through it. \"Press ✕\" or \"Press Enter/Click\", following the last input. Theme music. Any input leads to Main.\n- **Main menu** (over the dim theatre, the camera drifting):\n  - **ON CALL:** Continue or New Shift, then pick a difficulty.\n  - **OPERATING LOG:** replay cleared ops, showing best rank and a patient line. One chart at a time, flip with ←/→.\n  - **CONSULT**\n  - **SETTINGS**\n  - **ABOUT**\n- **Story scene:** set plus busts. ✕/Enter/click advances; hold △/Esc to skip. Typewriter text with gibberish voice, the speaker leaning in and the other dimmed. Occasional wide shots use full-body figures and the engine's `Timeline`.\n- **Briefing:** a clipboard chart: patient name, age, job, hook, the op's title stamped, and the one-line objective. Not a stats page. Then the camera dives from the OR-7 wide shot down onto the field (fly the three.js camera directly) with an iris transition.\n- **Operation HUD** (art pixels at 270 height):\n  - **Top strip, 20 tall:** VITALS number at scale 2 and a live EKG on the left, clock at centre, Composure at right.\n  - **Bottom strip, 32 tall:** speaker name and up to two lines of comm text.\n  - **Bottom-right:** the tool wheel (about 48 square), with the current tool in the centre, clickable.\n  - **Dose count** by the wheel. **Rating pop-ups** at scale 2 near the tip.\n  - **Comm bust:** a tiny real 3D bust of the speaker placed near the camera at the top-left corner, with `castShadow = false`, so in-op talk uses the same models and mouth animation.\n- **Results:** the chart drops in. Lines tally one at a time with ticks: time, vitals, technique, streak, mistakes. Rank stamp slams with shake, then a Reyes comment, then the patient's follow-up line for that rank.\n- **Pause (Options/Esc):** Resume, Retry Stage, Restart, Settings, **Dev Mode**, Quit to Menu. Use your own pause flag and stop stepping the sim. ✔ Don't use `engine.paused`: `update()` stops running and your menu dies. Disabled in a session.\n- **Settings** (own HUD screen, navigable by pad):\n  - Music (**10% default**), Sound, Voices.\n  - Button glyphs (PlayStation/Xbox), Aim Assist, Cursor Speed, Rumble, Gift Hold/Toggle.\n  - Look (engine looks), Pixel Size, Screen Shake, Reduce Flashes, Text Speed, Difficulty, Fullscreen, Reset.\n- **About/Credits:** paged, big text. Pages: Source Information; Testing Feedback; Engine Feedback; Prompt Feedback; Credits. All field labels and answers as your brief lists them. Data in `src/content/about.js`, filled in last. Credits condense the kit's `CREDITS.md` (engine MIT, three.js, Rapier, Kenney furniture CC0) and the game's own \"all art and audio written in code\".\n\n**Touch-only devices.** Detect before `Engine.start`: no `(any-pointer: fine)`, `maxTouchPoints > 0`, no gamepad. ✔ Phones report art like 136×276 at 8×, so the HUD would be a narrow column.\n\n- Show a DOM overlay with the exact text `Controller or keyboard required`, plus the engine's ⚙: ✔ `settings: { button: 'top-right' }` shows it on a phone profile and a tap opens the DOM panel.\n- `touch: false` always: ✔ no joystick appears.\n- The attract mode loops behind the message.\n- If a key is pressed or a pad connects, drop the gate and play normally.\n\n**Attract mode.** 10 s with no input on Title or any menu screen starts it. Input means a key, click, mouse move, stick beyond deadzone, pad button or touch; each resets the timer.\n\n- A looping reel of real sim segments of 20 to 30 s each, played by the bot with cheats (god vitals, free Composure): a talking-head snippet, Op 1 hooks, Op 2 scan and laser, Op 3 table swaps, Bone Mend, Introit with The Quiet, Second Look rewind, Lacrimosa, Dies Irae with Code Blue, then Pile-Up with four hands.\n- Banner `DEMO - PRESS ANY BUTTON`. Any input exits at once to Title and is swallowed.\n- It must never touch saves or settings.\n\n**Dev Mode** (from Pause; tabs on L1/R1, Q/E or click):\n\n- **BALANCE:** live sliders, Reset to Defaults (list in section 12).\n- **CHEATS:** God Vitals, Infinite Composure, Freeze Clock, Unlimited Mistakes, Unlock All.\n- **JUMP:** any op and stage, any story scene.\n- **ACTIONS:** Complete Stage, Win Op, Fail Op, Trigger Code Blue, Spawn (pool, bleeder, laceration, hook, strain), Copy Op JSON to console.\n- **VIEW:** hitbox overlay (entity circles and ids), Bot Plays (with skill slider), Sim Speed 0.1× to 3×, Frame Step, FPS and sim stats.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Art direction: what works\n\nThe engine's native style is low-poly 3D turned into pixel art. My mock of the heart arena with this recipe looked like a shipped game. Keep to these numbers unless you can beat them.\n\n**Framing.** `aspect: 'fill'` always. ✔ It gives no black bars:\n\n| Viewport | Art resolution | Scale |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1920×1080 | 480×270 | ×4 |\n| 3840×2160 | 480×270 | ×8 |\n| 1280×720 | 427×240 | ×3 |\n| 1024×768 | 342×256 | ×3 |\n| 800×600 | 400×300 | ×2 |\n| 600×400 | 600×400 | ×1 |\n\nWithout it, 1280×720 letterboxes to 960×540. Lay out all HUD from anchors.\n\n**The look** (✔ crisp outlines on tools and creatures, none on tissue):\n```js\nconst LOOK = (sat = 1, vig = .3, spread = 0) => ({\n  scene: [{ id: 'vignette', params: { intensity: vig } }, { id: 'adjust', params: { saturation: sat, contrast: 1 } }, { id: 'chromatic', params: { spread } }],\n  actors: { pixel: { size: 1, outline: .85, crease: .2 }, filters: [] },\n  environment: { pixel: { size: 1, outline: 0, crease: 0 }, filters: [] },\n});\n```\nThe split look renders two passes (about a third of the frame rate on software WebGPU here). That's fine: your brief puts performance out of scope. `sixteen_bit` dithers the whole frame and hurts readability ✔. Tag every tool, hand, strain and character with `setLookLayer(obj, 'actors')`.\n\n**Camera in surgery:** `{ preset: 'fixed', position: [0, 9.6, 3.1], target: [0, 0, 0.1], fov: 44, minZoom: 1, maxZoom: 1 }`.\n\n- ✔ Without the min/max lock the mouse wheel zooms the \"fixed\" camera, and wheel is our tool cycle.\n- ✔ Enter and WASD don't disturb a fixed rig.\n- ✔ Move the camera for parallax, dives and whip-pans by setting `ctx.camera.camera.position` and `.lookAt()` each frame; it sticks and `rayAt` follows. Add ±0.25 units of drift toward the tip.\n- For narrow windows multiply the camera's distance by `max(1, (16/9) / aspect)`.\n\n**Lighting.**\n\n- Field ✔: sun intensity 1.0 from `[.25, 1, .35]`, ambient 0.55 warm white (`0xfff0e0`), one point light at `[0, 5.2, .4]`, intensity 5, radius 15. Much more than that washes the tissue out.\n- OR-7 wide ✔: sun 0.35, ambient 0.28 cool (`0x8fa8c8`), lamp point light over the table at intensity 14, radius 7, a monitor glow. A dark room with a pool of light is the mood.\n- Never `new PointLight`; use `ctx.lights`.\n\n**The tissue canvas** is the game's signature. Each table has a 480×270 RGBA `DataTexture` on a 192×108 `PlaneGeometry` in `toonMaterial(PALETTE.white, { map })` with `receiveShadow`.\n\n- ✔ Copying the base into the buffer and painting 60 blood discs measured about 0.5 ms a frame.\n- Mapping ✔: `px = (x / 16 + .5) · W`, `py = (z / 9 + .5) · H`, and **flip the plane's UV v** (`uv.setY(i, 1 - uv.getY(i))`), or the paint lands mirrored.\n- Set `magFilter`/`minFilter` Nearest and `needsUpdate` after each paint.\n- Each frame: write the prebuilt base into the buffer, then paint scars, pools, wounds, stitches, gel and burns from sim state. Displace the mesh by `heightAt` plus heartbeat, breathing and bulges, then `computeVertexNormals()`.\n\nBase painting recipe (✔ the look, shown for the heart; each arena has its own ramp and shape):\n```js\nconst BAYER = [0,8,2,10,12,4,14,6,3,11,1,9,15,7,13,5];\nconst RAMP = [0x3c0d24, 0x5e1430, 0x8a1f38, 0xb5343f, 0xd65c4f];      // dark to light, 5 steps\n// per texel: m = shape mask (0 outside the organ); light = 0.25 + 0.75*m + (fbm(x*.9, z*.9) - .5)*.9 + tilt;\n// index = floor(clamp(light)*5 + BAYER[(px&3) + (py&3)*4]/16*.9 - .2) into RAMP (ordered dither between bands)\n// outside the organ: a dark cavity colour (0x1c0a18) with noise blotches of RAMP[0]\n// then: fat blobs (0xe9c46a) where fbm(x*1.6, z*2.4) > .66 near edges\n//       vessels: random-walk branches (heading += noise*.55, step .09, width 2 then 1, branch at 4.5%), arteries 0xf08a5d, veins 0x2e1a52\n//       wet sheen: a few hundred single 0xf6d0c0 texels on the light-facing side\n```\n\n| Arena | Ramp feel, shape |\n|---|---|\n| forearm | tan skin ramp, hair flecks, teal drape window |\n| stomach | pink-salmon, folded rugae lines |\n| 3 tables | one skin ramp each, small windows |\n| bone | dark muscle with a white bone silhouette |\n| liver | deep maroon, two big lobes |\n| kidney bed | fat-yellow bed, kidney bean mesh (plum to red tween) |\n| lung | grey-pink, dotted alveoli, breathing |\n| heart | the recipe above |\n| whole chest | ribs, lung and heart together |\n| spine | pale ivory and cool shadow |\n\nFrame every arena with raised teal drapes (boxes, `y` 0.4), steel clamps and retractors. Pools, blood and wounds use 2 or 3 flat colours with animated sparkle texels, plus particles for droplets, smoke and foam (`ctx.particles.register`; sizes are whole art pixels).\n\n**The hand and instruments.** Each is `model()` data with the tip at the origin, pointing −Z. A gloved hand plus forearm from below the frame sells first-person presence, and its cast shadow gives depth ✔.\n\n```js\nexport const handDef = model({ id:'glove-hand', about:'Gloved surgeon hand gripping a shaft, wrist toward +Z', tags:['character','hand'], floats:true,\n  palette:{ glove:'sky', fold:'blue', sleeve:'teal' }, parts:[\n  { name:'palm', box:[.72,.3,.8], at:[0,0,0], c:'glove' }, { name:'knuck', box:[.74,.16,.14], at:[0,.12,-.34], c:'fold' },\n  ...[-.27,-.09,.09,.27].flatMap((x,i)=>[{ name:`f${i}a`, box:[.16,.16,.34], at:[x,.05,-.56], rot:[18,0,0], c:'glove' },{ name:`f${i}b`, box:[.15,.15,.26], at:[x,-.09,-.76], rot:[58,0,0], c:'glove' }]),\n  { name:'thumb', box:[.18,.18,.5], at:[-.44,-.04,-.26], rot:[10,-28,0], c:'glove' },\n  { name:'cuff', cyl:[.62,.62,.3], at:[0,0,.54], rot:[90,0,0], c:'fold' }, { name:'wrist', cyl:[.56,1.6,.56], at:[0,0,1.46], rot:[90,0,0], c:'glove' },\n  { name:'sleeve', cyl:[.8,2.6,.8], at:[0,0,3.4], rot:[90,0,0], c:'sleeve' } ]});\n```\n\n- ✔ Placement that read well: tool at `(x, surface + .05, z)`, rotation `(-.5, -.7, 0)`; hand at `tip + (.88, 1.1, 1.25)`, rotation `(-.46, -.72, .2)`.\n- Seats 2 to 4 enter from other corners. Glove colour follows the seat: palette `red`, `blue`, `green`, `sand` in 3D; `info.players[i].color` exactly on the HUD (`hud.text` colours take numbers).\n- Give each tool a distinct silhouette: forceps with moving jaws, curved needle plus thread (try `RopeMesh` with `ropeLine`, and check it reads), drain wand, syringe with moving plunger, laser pen, scanner disc (`hologramMaterial`), gel bottle.\n\n**Busts: the anime talking head.** Build the face and hair from `slab` outlines. ✔ This gives a real anime silhouette in the engine's style at about 150 art pixels tall. Put the head in a named pivot, and the mouth, brows and lids in their own pivots.\n\n```js\nconst FACE = [[-.46,.5],[.46,.5],[.5,.05],[.42,-.28],[.2,-.56],[0,-.68],[-.2,-.56],[-.42,-.28],[-.5,.05]];\nconst FRINGE = [[-.56,.42],[-.6,0],[-.44,.16],[-.4,-.08],[-.22,.24],[-.06,.02],[.06,.26],[.24,.04],[.34,.26],[.46,-.1],[.6,.02],[.56,.42],[.34,.66],[0,.74],[-.34,.66]];\n// parts (head group at [0,1.62,0], pivot:true, name:'head'):\n// { name:'skull', box:[.9,.92,.72], at:[0,.1,-.12] }, { name:'face', slab:FACE, depth:.26, at:[0,0,.14] },\n// { name:'hairfront', slab:FRINGE, depth:.16, at:[0,.22,.26] }, { name:'hairback', box:[.98,.86,.5], at:[0,.2,-.34] },\n// eyes at z≈.28: white box .22×.16, pupil box .12×.16 at z .30; brow box .28×.05 at y .2, rot z -18 (mirror x); nose box; mouth in a pivot group\n```\n\n- ✔ Set `receiveShadow = castShadow = false` on bust meshes or shadow acne scatters triangles over the face.\n- Camera for a close-up ✔: `position [.2, 1.75, 5.1]`, `target [0, 1.42, 0]`, `fov 30`.\n- ✔ A half-`ball` fills its box, so its base sits at `at.y − h/2`: the first cap I built covered the eyes.\n- Emotions are a small pose table per character: neutral, stern, shock, sad, smile, angry, panic (brow rotation and height, lid scale, mouth scale, head tilt). Add a few toggled extras: sweat drop, blush, tear, glasses glint.\n- Mouth scale follows voice syllables, blinks every 2 to 5 s, slight idle sway.\n- Draw big white reaction marks and speed-line flourishes on the HUD for comic beats.\n\n**Full-body figures for wide shots.** ⚠ The bundled hero is a red-capped, moustached plumber in overalls: **do not show `HERO_MODEL`.** But ✔ a `model()` whose pivots carry the hero rig's joint names plays every `HERO_CLIPS` clip through `compileClips(HERO_CLIPS, HERO_RIG, build.object)` and a three.js `AnimationMixer`. I tested Idle, Walk, Wave, Sit and Shout; there are also Victory, Hurt, HitReact, Death, LieIdle, Grab, Triumph and more. The figure faces +Z; its right is −X.\n\n```js\nconst arm=(s,x)=>({ group:[{ name:`upper${s}`, box:[.11,.25,.11], at:[0,-.12,0], c:'scrub' },\n  { group:[{ name:`fore${s}`, box:[.1,.23,.1], at:[0,-.11,0], c:'skin' },\n    { group:[{ name:`glove${s}`, box:[.12,.13,.12], at:[0,-.06,0], c:'glove' }], at:[0,-.23,0], name:`Hand${s}`, pivot:true }], at:[0,-.25,0], name:`Forearm${s}`, pivot:true }],\n  at:[x,.36,0], name:`Arm${s}`, pivot:true });\nconst leg=(s,x)=>({ group:[{ name:`thigh${s}`, box:[.15,.3,.15], at:[0,-.15,0], c:'scrub' },\n  { group:[{ name:`shin${s}`, box:[.13,.22,.13], at:[0,-.11,0], c:'scrub' },\n    { group:[{ name:`shoe${s}`, box:[.15,.1,.28], at:[0,-.05,.06], c:'shoe' }], at:[0,-.22,0], name:`Foot${s}`, pivot:true }], at:[0,-.3,0], name:`Shin${s}`, pivot:true }],\n  at:[x,0,0], name:`Leg${s}`, pivot:true });\n// parts: [{ group:[ { name:'hips', box:[.36,.18,.22], at:[0,.02,0], c:'scrub' },\n//   { group:[ { name:'chest', box:[.38,.42,.24], at:[0,.22,0], c:'scrub' },\n//     { group:[ skull, cap, mask, eyes ], at:[0,.44,0], name:'Head', pivot:true }, arm('R',-.25), arm('L',.25) ], at:[0,.1,0], name:'Torso', pivot:true },\n//   leg('R',-.14), leg('L',.14) ], at:[0,.62,0], name:'Pelvis', pivot:true }]\n```\nVary cap, hair, coat and height per character. Masked surgeons read very well at distance ✔.\n\n**Sets** (each a `model()`/mesh group with a lighting recipe): OR-7 (table, patient under drape, lamp arm, monitor on a stand, instrument tray, gallery glass, doors), scrub room (sinks), Chief's office (desk, window with `Precipitation` rain and harbour lights), ward (beds, `clothGrid` curtains), corridor, Foundation atrium (white, gold, flowers), helipad roof at night in the rain.\n\n- **Generic props** come from the `kenney-furniture` pack (beds, sinks, desks, chairs, cabinets, screens, lamps; search `LIBRARY.md`). Recolour them to steel and hospital tones with `buildModel(id, { catalog: kit, palette: {...} })`; they arrive bright yellow-wood ✔.\n- ✔ **Packs in one file:** put `window.__PIXEL_ASSETS__ = { 'packs/kenney-furniture.json': 'data:application/json;base64,…' }` in a classic script before the module, and `await loadPack('packs/kenney-furniture.json')` works from `file://`.\n- Nice touches if cheap: a `RenderView` live monitor in OR-7, a `Mirror` in the scrub room.\n\n**Check your models.** `node check.mjs --sheets src/content/models/index.js` ✔ draws every def and warns about z-fighting and floating parts. Models need `about` and `tags`; busts and tools need `floats: true`.\n\n**Game feel.** `engine.hitstop`, `engine.shake.add`, `engine.screen.flash/shockwave/cover/reveal`, `Squash` on grabs and hits, rating pop-ups, stamp slams, lamp flicker at low vitals. Honour the Screen Shake and Reduce Flashes settings.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Audio: everything written in code\n\n**Music is 10% by default.** ✔ The engine's default is 0.6, stored in `localStorage['pixel-engine:audio']`. On boot: if that key is absent, call `audio.setVolume('music', 0.1)`, which also stores it. A test asserts this on a fresh profile.\n\n**Voices: Animalese/Simlish gibberish.**\n\n- Pre-render syllables in pure JS at boot: a glottal pulse through two or three formants (`src/audio/voice.js`, testable in Node). Use 3 timbres × 5 vowels × 3 consonant onsets, about 120 ms each.\n- ✔ Wrap the PCM in a WAV header, make a base64 data URL and call `await ctx.audio.load('syl-a', url)`. Then `ctx.audio.play('syl-a', { pitch, volume, pan })`: it works from `file://`, runs through the engine's buses and respects mute.\n- Letters pick syllables deterministically; punctuation shapes rhythm and pitch (\"!\" up and louder, \"?\" rising, \"...\" slow).\n- Each cast member has `{ timbre, basePitch, speed, range }` per the cast table. Reaction barks in surgery use the same system.\n- The Voices slider scales `volume` per play, since the engine has only master, sfx and music channels.\n\n**Sound effects: `SoundDef` data via `ctx.audio.register`.**\n\n- Tools: drain slurp loop (`audio.loop`, pitch follows force), forceps click, hook pop, dish tink, scalpel slice, suture tick (note scale), knot, laser buzz loop, sizzle, scanner ping, gel fizz loop, syringe draw, inject whoosh.\n- Monitors and crisis: EKG beep (pitch and rate follow vitals), alarm, flatline, defib charge whine, CLEAR thump.\n- UI: move, confirm, back, stamp slam, rating chimes.\n- Gifts: heartbeat and inhale, rewind tape.\n- Strains: one signature sound each, plus the knock itself.\n- Room: rain, harbour horn and ship bells under story scenes.\n\n**Music: engine `Song` data (chiptune sequencer), all original compositions.** Don't quote any source music or any real requiem.\n\n- Title theme: a slow, sad triangle lead with a soft pulse.\n- Ward/lounge: tired light jazz.\n- `or-calm`, `or-tense` and `or-critical`: same key and tempo family so switching at bar lines sounds intentional.\n- Four boss themes with saw \"choir\" pads. Dies Irae's tempo follows the heart: restart with new `bpm` at bar lines every few steps.\n- Op 9's silence, then a swell. Op 10 sparse and gentle. Results fanfare and sad variant. Credits.\n\n`MusicDirector` changes tracks at bar lines from vitals and stage. `loadGame` clears music and loops, so have the director restart on each stage.\n\n---\n\n## 11. Architecture\n\n```\npixel-engine.js check.mjs GUIDE.md API.md …   the kit, unchanged, as it unzips\nindex.html, game.js          game.js exports createGame() and starts the engine only when `document` exists\nsrc/core/     config.js (defaults + live values), rng.js, save.js, meta.js (title, tagline)\nsrc/sim/      op.js, tools.js, entities.js, strains/*.js, scoring.js, bot.js, codec.js, campaign.js\nsrc/content/  ops/*.js, scenes/*.js, lines.js, cast.js, arenas.js, songs.js, sfx.js, icons.js, about.js, models/*.js\nsrc/view/     field.js, hands.js, strains/*.js, sets.js, bust.js, figure.js, fx.js\nsrc/ui/       hud.js, prompts.js, menu.js, then one file per screen\nsrc/stages/   title.js story.js briefing.js operation.js results.js log.js consult.js card.js attract.js\nsrc/input/    devices.js, cursor.js\nsrc/net/      session.js, host.js, client.js\nsrc/audio/    voice.js, director.js\nvendor/       session.js, harness.html, bridge.js, round.js (from the hub, unmodified)\ntools/build.mjs\ntests/        run.mjs, *.test.mjs, browser/*, balance.mjs\ndocs/AUTHORING.md            how to add an op, scene, strain or character\n```\n\n**The one rule that makes everything else possible: `src/sim` and non-model content import nothing from the engine, the DOM or the clock.** The sim is plain data plus pure functions: `sim = createOp(def, { seed, seats, difficulty, config })`, `step(sim, inputsBySeat)` at 60 Hz, `events = drainEvents(sim)`.\n\n- Input per seat is `{ x, z, tool, use, gift, steady, drop, … }`.\n- Randomness comes from its own seeded generator, never `Math.random`.\n- State must survive `structuredClone`. This one rule gives you:\n  - The Second Look.\n  - Determinism: same seed plus inputs gives the same hash.\n  - Tests in Node in milliseconds.\n  - The bot.\n  - A hub server copy with no renderer.\n  - Network snapshots.\n\n**Stages.** Each screen is a `Game` class, swapped with `engine.loadGame(new XStage(args))` under `engine.screen.cover/reveal`. A persistent `App` singleton holds save, settings, devices, config and the director. Set `status()` meaningfully (`op5 stage=2 vitals=64 t=121 score=3400`) and put test handles in `ready(ctx)` (`window.__GAME__ = { app, sim, goto, config }`). In solo, step the sim from `fixedUpdate`; draw in `update`. Cosmetic randomness comes from `ctx.random.fork('fx')`.\n\n**Content is data**, so the rest of the game can be built with ordinary tools (JSON-safe, hot-editable):\n\n```js\nexport default { id:'op1', title:'ELEVEN HOOKS', arena:'forearm', surgeon:'ilya', gifts:[], tools:['drain','forceps','suture','gel','syringe'],\n  patient:{ name:'TOMASZ DOLAN', age:52, job:'TRAWLER DECKHAND', hook:\"HIS DAUGHTER'S WEDDING IS SATURDAY.\",\n            followUp:{ S:'He walked her down the aisle. Dry eyes.', C:'He danced badly. She cried anyway.' } },\n  time:240, vitals:{ start:85, drain:.10 }, doses:3, music:'or-calm', par:4200,\n  stages:[\n    { id:'pools', say:'reyes.drainFirst', hint:'drain',\n      spawn:[{ k:'pool', id:'p1', at:[-3,.6], r:1.6 }, { k:'hook', id:'h1', at:[-3,.9], hiddenBy:'p1', arc:.8, pull:1.2 }],\n      until:{ clear:['pool'] },\n      on:{ vitalsBelow:{ 50:{ say:'reyes.stabilize', unlock:'syringe' } } } },\n    …\n  ] };\n```\n\n- Entity kinds (`pool, hook, nick, laceration, incision, tumor, polyp, prop, magnet, bleeder, clamp, vessel, fragment, organ, mask, strain:*`) register their tool handlers in `entities.js`.\n- `until` takes `clear`, `flag`, `all` or `time`. Commands: `say, spawn, remove, unlock, setDrain, music, camera, flag, codeBlue`.\n- Scenes are data too: `{ id, set, music, beats:[{ who, emo, say, cam, cue }] }`. Reaction pools live in `lines.js` (`reyes.mistake[]`, `reyes.clean[]`, `reyes.lowVitals[]`).\n\n**The bot** (`src/sim/bot.js`) reads sim state and produces seat input, with `skill` 0 to 1 scaling speed, path noise, reaction delay and judgement (syringe when low, gifts when useful). It knows a strategy per entity kind. It is one piece of code with four jobs: **attract mode, the whole-game test playthrough, the balance report and the Op 9 partner.** Build it early.\n\n**Engine facts to save you time**\n\n- ✔ `update()` does not run while `engine.paused` is true; it does run at `timeScale = 0`.\n- `loadGame` clears HUD, music, loops, particles and lights; it keeps Input, volumes and look.\n- `engine.settings.open()` is a mouse-driven DOM panel that pauses the engine: use it only on the touch-only path; build your own Settings.\n- Start options: `aspect:'fill'`, `touch:false`, `settings:{ button:false, key: inSession ? false : '<slug>' }`, `background`, plus `withUrlOptions` for review flags.\n- Saves: guarded `localStorage` under a versioned key. In a session the client hands you an empty store.\n- `game.js` must import cleanly in Node for `check.mjs --headless`: guard `document`, `navigator.getGamepads` and `localStorage`.\n- Own URL flags outside a session, for tests: `?op= &stage= &diff= &seed= &bot= &god= &attract= &dev= &scene=`.\n\n---\n\n## 12. Balance\n\n**Dev Mode sliders (live, with Reset to Defaults).** All in `config.js`:\n\n- vitals drain ×, bleed drain, mistake penalty, max mistakes, time limit ×\n- cursor speed, steady factor, aim assist, tool tolerance ×\n- drain rate, laser burn time, syringe dose\n- Composure gain per CLEAN, Quiet slow factor, Quiet drain, Second Look cost and seconds\n- strain speed ×, strain HP ×, Dies Irae base BPM\n- Code Blue zone width, co-op scale per seat\n\n**`node tests/balance.mjs`** runs each op on the bot at skills 0.4, 0.7 and 1.0 and prints time used, final vitals, mistakes and rank. Targets on Resident:\n\n| Bot skill | Should | |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0 (idle, no input) | fail every op | |\n| 0.4 | clear Ops 1 to 3, may lose bosses | a nervous beginner |\n| 0.7 | clear all, mostly B or A, at least 20% clock left outside bosses | a decent player |\n| 1.0 | S on all | sets `par` |\n\n---\n\n## 13. Testing\n\nOne command: `node tests/run.mjs` prints only failures and one count line. An optional filter (`sim`, `content`, `browser`, `hub`) lets you rerun only what you changed.\n\n**Node (fast, most tests):**\n\n- Each tool's rules, success and mistake paths.\n- Every op: idle fails; bot 0.7 clears; determinism hash stable; retry-from-stage works.\n- Code Blue paths, The Quiet's time scale, The Second Look's exact restore.\n- Scoring and rank bounds.\n- Slider apply and reset.\n- Codec round trip and sizes at each op's peak.\n- **Whole-game scripted playthrough:** `campaign.js` driven by the bot through every scene and op to credits, with save and unlock checks.\n\n**Content lint:**\n\n- Cast and sets referenced exist; every tool used; all text fits two wrapped lines at 342 art pixels wide; every character is in the font's set; glyph tokens valid.\n- No `TODO` or placeholder strings; About has every field.\n- No forbidden source names.\n- `check.mjs --sheets` clean of problems.\n\n**Browser (Chromium, one or two at a time):** launch args ✔ `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader --autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required`.\n\nSoftware WebGPU runs at 5 to 30 fps here; prefer the sim's state and `engine.step()` over waiting, and use a 960×540 viewport for logic. A pad stub:\n```js\nwindow.__pad = { connected:true, mapping:'standard', index:0, id:'stub', axes:[0,0,0,0], buttons:Array.from({length:17},()=>({pressed:false,value:0})), vibrationActuator:{ playEffect:()=>Promise.resolve('complete') } };\nnavigator.getGamepads = () => [window.__pad, null, null, null];   // add_init_script\n```\nCover:\n\n- The built page from `file://`: boots, no errors. Outside a session `AIHub.active` is false and `AIHub.seeded` is not true. Enter, Space, Enter, Space then still draws (the hub's own \"on its own\" check).\n- Fresh profile: music slider 0.1.\n- Menu navigation by pad stub, keys and mouse (hover moves focus).\n- Prompts switch with the last device; the Xbox option swaps glyphs.\n- A real drain and forceps action by mouse and by pad stub (the sim state changes at the aimed spot).\n- Attract: idle 10 s starts it; key and pad each exit; save untouched.\n- Touch-only with `p.devices['Pixel 7']`: the exact text, the ⚙, no joystick, attract runs.\n- Pause, then Dev Mode: a slider changes live config; reset restores it.\n- Couch co-op with two stub pads: two independent tips.\n- `engine.errors` and `gpuErrors` empty throughout.\n\n**Sound:** render syllables and `SoundDef`s (`renderSound`) in Node: non-silent, finite. In the page, `audio.counts` rise while talking. An `AnalyserNode` level check on one voice line.\n\n**Hub:** copy `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` beside the built page in `dist/`. Serve **`python3 -u -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1`**. ✔ The `-u` matters: when you read the port from a pipe without it, the line never arrives and your script hangs (this cost me about fifteen minutes). Stop that server by its PID. Run these with launch args plus `--no-sandbox`, a 1600×1000 viewport, and wait for `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`:\n```\nharness.html?game=game.html&auto=1&players=2\nharness.html?game=game.html&auto=1&players=3&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5\nharness.html?game=game.html&auto=1&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5\nharness.html?game=game.html&auto=1&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&scenario=host-leave\nharness.html?game=game.html&auto=1&players=2&scenario=server\n```\nAll must give `window.__hubCheck.pass === true`.\n\n**Kit tools** ✔ all work here after `npm install playwright@1.63.0` in the dev folder (about 1 to 3 s each): `node check.mjs` (serves on an OS-picked 127.0.0.1 port), `node check.mjs --headless game.js --keys …`, `node check.mjs --sheets …`.\n\n**Screenshots only for what scripts can't judge**, at 1920×1080: each arena, each set, each bust, title, results, HUD readability. Look at them. Blank WebGPU canvases can happen; ✔ here `page.screenshot` captured every frame fine.\n\n---\n\n## 14. Build and packaging\n\n`tools/build.mjs` ✔ (this exact recipe gave a 6 MB page that booted from `file://` in about 1 s on software WebGPU):\n\n```js\nexecFileSync('esbuild', ['game.js','--bundle','--format=esm','--platform=browser','--target=es2022','--outfile=dist/bundle.js']);\nconst js = readFileSync('dist/bundle.js','utf8').replace(/<\\/script/gi,'<\\\\/script');\nconst session = readFileSync('vendor/session.js','utf8');           // verbatim: the hub compares it byte for byte\nconst pack = readFileSync('packs/kenney-furniture.json').toString('base64');\nconst html = `<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<script>\\n${session}\\n</script>\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>${TITLE} — ${TAGLINE}</title> …description, theme-color, data-URL icon, hub:* tags…\n</head><body><div id=\"app\"></div>\n<script>window.__PIXEL_ASSETS__={'packs/kenney-furniture.json':'data:application/json;base64,${pack}'};</script>\n<script type=\"module\">\\n${js}\\n</script></body></html>`;\n```\n\n- The output name comes from your brief: one constant at the top of the script. Write `dist/game.html` for the tests and a copy where your brief wants the deliverable.\n- Don't minify the HTML or touch the session client's text.\n- Also add `hub:type` Game, `hub:source` for the source, and an emblem icon as a data URL.\n- When you report research, say this plan's planner read the source's Wikipedia page, the hub's protocol and the engine kit, and ran engine spikes; add anything you did yourself.\n- For the exit-interview file your brief asks for, `aiHub.genre` is `Simulation`, `players` `1–4`, `series` `Trauma Center`. Good tags: `3d`, `pixel art`, `story`, `co-op`, `boss fights`, `comedy`.\n\n---\n\n## 15. Order of work\n\nBuild in this order. Keep the game running and the tests green after each step.\n\n1. **Skeleton.** Unzip the kit and move the contents of its `pixel-engine/` folder to the dev folder root. `npm install playwright@1.63.0` there. Then: build script, test runner, an empty stage booting from `file://`, music default, input devices with pad stub test.\n2. **One great op.** Sim core, tissue canvas, hand and tools, HUD, Drain, Forceps, Suture, Gel, Syringe, Op 1 playable on pad, mouse and keys. Make this feel wonderful before moving on.\n3. **All tools and the bot.** Scalpel, Laser, Scanner; Ops 2 and 3; Code Blue; The Quiet; bot and balance report; whole-op tests.\n4. **The drama.** Busts, figures, sets, story stage, voices, sound effects, music director, results, saves. Eps 1 to 3 flow end to end.\n5. **The shell.** Title, menus, prompts, settings, pause, Dev Mode, attract, touch gate, About.\n6. **Bosses and the rest.** Second Look, Bone Mend, transplant, Introit, Lacrimosa, Dies Irae, Libera Me, Do No Harm, all scenes, campaign playthrough test.\n7. **Consult.** Couch first (it proves the seats), then session, card, net, harness passes.\n8. **Polish and balance.** Juice, feel, per-arena art, tune against the targets, full screenshot pass at 1080p, `docs/AUTHORING.md`.\n9. **Finish.** Fill in About and your chat reply and exit-interview file as your brief says.\n\n**If you run short, cut whole content rather than leave anything half-made** (the brief forbids stubs). Cut in this order:\n\n1. The `RenderView` and `Mirror` touches.\n2. Extra session fights (keep Pile-Up).\n3. Op 3's third table.\n4. Lacrimosa's crawling phase.\n5. Op 6's cold-time bar.\n\nNever cut: Ops 1, 2, 5, 8, 9; both gifts; Code Blue; attract; Dev Mode; hub conformance; couch co-op.\n\n## 16. Done means\n\n| The brief asks for | Where |\n|---|---|\n| Genre and perspective chosen | §1 |\n| Title by the brief's method | Yours, `src/core/meta.js` |\n| One HTML, engine unmodified, session client verbatim | §14 |\n| Native art plus new assets | §9 |\n| Native animation plus new animations | §6, §9 (`HERO_CLIPS` on custom rigs, procedural tools) |\n| All audio in code, gibberish voices, music at 10% | §10 |\n| AI Hub integration and the game on its own | §7, §13 |\n| Feature-complete demo showing every mechanic | §3, §5, §6 |\n| World, characters, themes, tone, writing style | §2 |\n| Infrastructure for more content with normal tools | §11, `docs/AUTHORING.md`, Dev Mode's Copy Op JSON |\n| Dev mode from pause, live sliders, reset | §8, §12 |\n| Attract after 10 s, any input exits | §8 |\n| Controller-first at 10 feet, native keyboard and mouse, prompts by last input, Xbox option | §4, §8 |\n| No dense data screens | §8 |\n| Touch-only gate, settings button, attract runs | §8 |\n| Tests behind one command, whole-game playthrough | §13 |\n| No TODOs or placeholders | §13 lint |\n| Source Information, Testing, Engine and Prompt Feedback in chat and About; exit interview | §8, §14, your brief |\n","numLines":515,"startLine":380,"totalLines":894}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_015UjUJaBZiD7RJXsU9A6oyH","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
