{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018H74VvCunqH3QRkJ8UxcC8","type":"tool_result","content":"examples:\nlooks.html\nlooks.js\nmarket-models.js\nmarket.html\nmarket.js\nside-scroller.html\nside-scroller.js\ntop-down.html\ntop-down.js\ntotal 2892\ndrwxr-xr-x  2 micha micha    4096 Nov  5 16:20 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 11 micha micha    4096 Nov  5 16:21 ..\n-rw-r--r--  1 micha micha    2886 Nov  5 16:20 index.json\n-rw-r--r--  1 micha micha  506467 Nov  5 16:20 kenney-castle.json\n-rw-r--r--  1 micha micha  675400 Nov  5 16:20 kenney-furniture.json\n-rw-r--r--  1 micha micha  133943 Nov  5 16:20 kenney-mini-dungeon.json\n-rw-r--r--  1 micha micha 1151824 Nov  5 16:20 kenney-nature.json\n-rw-r--r--  1 micha micha  238973 Nov  5 16:20 kenney-tiny-dungeon.json\n-rw-r--r--  1 micha micha  229660 Nov  5 16:20 kenney-tiny-town.json\n{\n  \"name\": \"pixel-engine\",\n  \"version\": \"0.46.0\",\n  \"build\": \"2026-11-02 f75d4a6\",\n  \"source\": \"https://github.com/michaelcrosato/riftlight\",\n  \"latest\": \"https://github.com/michaelcrosato/riftlight/releases/latest/download/pixel-engine.zip\",\n  \"releases\": \"https://github.com/michaelcrosato/riftlight/releases\",\n  \"entry\": \"pixel-engine.js\",\n  \"readFirst\": [\n    \"README.md\",\n    \"GUIDE.md\"\n  ],\n  \"starter\": {\n    \"page\": \"index.html\",\n    \"script\": \"game.js\"\n  },\n  \"examples\": [\n    \"examples/side-scroller.html\",\n    \"examples/top-down.html\",\n    \"examples/looks.html\",\n    \"examples/market.html\"\n  ],\n  \"assets\": {\n    \"guide\": \"ASSETS.md\",\n    \"library\": \"LIBRARY.md\",\n    \"index\": \"library.json\",\n    \"packs\": \"packs/index.json\",\n    \"credits\": \"CREDITS.md\"\n  },\n  \"builtinModels\": [\n220:- `settings?: { button?: TouchCorner | boolean; key?: string | false }`: The player's settings (`engine.settings`): look, pixel art, pixel size, quality, frame rate, sound and debug info, in a panel the ⚙ button opens. `button`: its corner (default, or true: 'top-right'; on a mouse it shows while the pointer moves), or false for n…\n221:- `touch?: boolean`: On-screen joystick + buttons. Default: auto (coarse pointer), or ?touch=1 / ?touch=0.\n594:- `rayAt(x: number, y: number, origin: Vector3, dir: Vector3): void`: The ray through screen point (x, y) in normalised device coordinates (−1..1, y up, as `input.pointer` gives them): where it starts (on the near plane) and its unit direction. For picking things with the mouse, or aiming at it. An orthographic rig stands far b…\n625:Eyes of the character: mouse look (click to lock the pointer) or Q/E to turn. No zoom.\n2253:A pointer button pressed or let go (`Input.buttonEvents`): its key, and where the pointer was (normalised device coordinates).\n2275:KEYMAP). Change `input.gamepadButtons` to remap. Indices follow the W3C \"standard\" layout:\n2289:Keyboard + pointer + gamepad input.\n2293:  right stick feeds the pointer delta (camera look), buttons press key codes\n2294:  (`gamepadButtons`). Polled once per frame by the engine (`beginFrame`).\n2295:- Pointer: accumulated movement per frame (while a button is held or the pointer is\n2296:  locked), wheel delta per frame, optional pointer lock (first-person). Mouse buttons on\n2303:- `readonly mouseDelta: { x: number; y: number; }`: Pointer movement this frame, in CSS pixels (drag or pointer lock).\n2304:- `readonly pointer: { x: number; y: number; over: boolean; touch: boolean; }`: Where the pointer last was over the canvas, in normalised device coordinates (−1..1, y up: `camera.rayAt(pointer.x, pointer.y, …)` turns it into a ray), and whether it is over it now. Under pointer lock it is the screen's centre (the crosshair).\n2306:- `wantsPointerLock: boolean`: When true, clicking the canvas requests pointer lock (first-person / free camera).\n2308:- `readonly padAxis: { x: number; y: number; }`: Gamepad left stick after the deadzone, -1..1 (y = forward).\n2310:- `readonly preventKeys: Set<string>`: Extra key codes whose browser default is blocked (arrows and Space always are): a game's own F1 / F2 / Tab panels, so the browser's help page or focus change doesn't fire.\n2311:- `gamepadButtons: Record<number, string>`: Gamepad button index → key code (defaults: GAMEPAD_BUTTONS).\n2313:- `gamepadLookSpeed: number`: Right stick look speed: pointer pixels per second at full tilt.\n2315:- `get playing: boolean`: True while a replay drives input (`engine.replay()`): keyboard, pointer and wheel events, `setKey` / `setPointer` / `setButtons` / `addPointer` (touch buttons, scripts) and `send` are ignored, and `playBefore` / `playAfter` set everything.\n2317:- `attachPointer(el: HTMLElement): void`: Listen for pointer input on the game canvas. Only pointers that went down on the canvas drive the camera (so a touch joystick doesn't orbit it). Two canvas touches pinch to zoom (emitted as wheel ticks).\n2319:- `release(): void`: Let go of everything held (keys, gamepad buttons, sticks, pointer buttons); queued presses stay.\n2320:- `reset(): void`: Forget held keys, presses, sticks and pointer movement (e.g. when a level loads).\n2322:- `get pointerLocked: boolean`\n2328:- `state(): InputState`: Held keys, queued presses and the pointer as data (`engine.snapshot()`), between frames.\n2335:- `setPointer(x: number, y: number, down?: boolean): void`: Test hook: put the pointer at (x, y) in normalised device coordinates, pressed or not.\n2338:- `get buttonEvents: readonly ButtonEvent[]`: This frame's pointer button presses and releases, in order, each with where the pointer was: a drag shorter than a frame (a script's) still starts where it started and ends where it ended. Recorded with the frame. UI that acts on clicks reads these; play read…\n2342:- `addPointer(dx: number, dy: number, wheel = 0): void`: Test hook: inject pointer movement / wheel for the next frame.\n2343:- `snapshot(dt: number, last?: SnapshotMemory): InputFrame`: This frame's input as data (after `beginFrame`), for a recording. `last` is the frame before: unchanged held keys, pointer and gamepad connection are left out.\n2345:- `playAfter(f: InputFrame): void`: Replay, after `beginFrame` (which polled no gamepads): sticks, pointer, wheel, gamepad connection.\n2350:Optional fields are left out when empty or zero; `held` and `pointer` also when unchanged","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"75cb47e1-b6a0-4fd4-af20-38b42f9600a5","uuid":"64743eff-c518-475b-b03e-b6a0ba540a0c","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:33:43.687Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"examples:\nlooks.html\nlooks.js\nmarket-models.js\nmarket.html\nmarket.js\nside-scroller.html\nside-scroller.js\ntop-down.html\ntop-down.js\ntotal 2892\ndrwxr-xr-x  2 micha micha    4096 Nov  5 16:20 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 11 micha micha    4096 Nov  5 16:21 ..\n-rw-r--r--  1 micha micha    2886 Nov  5 16:20 index.json\n-rw-r--r--  1 micha micha  506467 Nov  5 16:20 kenney-castle.json\n-rw-r--r--  1 micha micha  675400 Nov  5 16:20 kenney-furniture.json\n-rw-r--r--  1 micha micha  133943 Nov  5 16:20 kenney-mini-dungeon.json\n-rw-r--r--  1 micha micha 1151824 Nov  5 16:20 kenney-nature.json\n-rw-r--r--  1 micha micha  238973 Nov  5 16:20 kenney-tiny-dungeon.json\n-rw-r--r--  1 micha micha  229660 Nov  5 16:20 kenney-tiny-town.json\n{\n  \"name\": \"pixel-engine\",\n  \"version\": \"0.46.0\",\n  \"build\": \"2026-11-02 f75d4a6\",\n  \"source\": \"https://github.com/michaelcrosato/riftlight\",\n  \"latest\": \"https://github.com/michaelcrosato/riftlight/releases/latest/download/pixel-engine.zip\",\n  \"releases\": \"https://github.com/michaelcrosato/riftlight/releases\",\n  \"entry\": \"pixel-engine.js\",\n  \"readFirst\": [\n    \"README.md\",\n    \"GUIDE.md\"\n  ],\n  \"starter\": {\n    \"page\": \"index.html\",\n    \"script\": \"game.js\"\n  },\n  \"examples\": [\n    \"examples/side-scroller.html\",\n    \"examples/top-down.html\",\n    \"examples/looks.html\",\n    \"examples/market.html\"\n  ],\n  \"assets\": {\n    \"guide\": \"ASSETS.md\",\n    \"library\": \"LIBRARY.md\",\n    \"index\": \"library.json\",\n    \"packs\": \"packs/index.json\",\n    \"credits\": \"CREDITS.md\"\n  },\n  \"builtinModels\": [\n220:- `settings?: { button?: TouchCorner | boolean; key?: string | false }`: The player's settings (`engine.settings`): look, pixel art, pixel size, quality, frame rate, sound and debug info, in a panel the ⚙ button opens. `button`: its corner (default, or true: 'top-right'; on a mouse it shows while the pointer moves), or false for n…\n221:- `touch?: boolean`: On-screen joystick + buttons. Default: auto (coarse pointer), or ?touch=1 / ?touch=0.\n594:- `rayAt(x: number, y: number, origin: Vector3, dir: Vector3): void`: The ray through screen point (x, y) in normalised device coordinates (−1..1, y up, as `input.pointer` gives them): where it starts (on the near plane) and its unit direction. For picking things with the mouse, or aiming at it. An orthographic rig stands far b…\n625:Eyes of the character: mouse look (click to lock the pointer) or Q/E to turn. No zoom.\n2253:A pointer button pressed or let go (`Input.buttonEvents`): its key, and where the pointer was (normalised device coordinates).\n2275:KEYMAP). Change `input.gamepadButtons` to remap. Indices follow the W3C \"standard\" layout:\n2289:Keyboard + pointer + gamepad input.\n2293:  right stick feeds the pointer delta (camera look), buttons press key codes\n2294:  (`gamepadButtons`). Polled once per frame by the engine (`beginFrame`).\n2295:- Pointer: accumulated movement per frame (while a button is held or the pointer is\n2296:  locked), wheel delta per frame, optional pointer lock (first-person). Mouse buttons on\n2303:- `readonly mouseDelta: { x: number; y: number; }`: Pointer movement this frame, in CSS pixels (drag or pointer lock).\n2304:- `readonly pointer: { x: number; y: number; over: boolean; touch: boolean; }`: Where the pointer last was over the canvas, in normalised device coordinates (−1..1, y up: `camera.rayAt(pointer.x, pointer.y, …)` turns it into a ray), and whether it is over it now. Under pointer lock it is the screen's centre (the crosshair).\n2306:- `wantsPointerLock: boolean`: When true, clicking the canvas requests pointer lock (first-person / free camera).\n2308:- `readonly padAxis: { x: number; y: number; }`: Gamepad left stick after the deadzone, -1..1 (y = forward).\n2310:- `readonly preventKeys: Set<string>`: Extra key codes whose browser default is blocked (arrows and Space always are): a game's own F1 / F2 / Tab panels, so the browser's help page or focus change doesn't fire.\n2311:- `gamepadButtons: Record<number, string>`: Gamepad button index → key code (defaults: GAMEPAD_BUTTONS).\n2313:- `gamepadLookSpeed: number`: Right stick look speed: pointer pixels per second at full tilt.\n2315:- `get playing: boolean`: True while a replay drives input (`engine.replay()`): keyboard, pointer and wheel events, `setKey` / `setPointer` / `setButtons` / `addPointer` (touch buttons, scripts) and `send` are ignored, and `playBefore` / `playAfter` set everything.\n2317:- `attachPointer(el: HTMLElement): void`: Listen for pointer input on the game canvas. Only pointers that went down on the canvas drive the camera (so a touch joystick doesn't orbit it). Two canvas touches pinch to zoom (emitted as wheel ticks).\n2319:- `release(): void`: Let go of everything held (keys, gamepad buttons, sticks, pointer buttons); queued presses stay.\n2320:- `reset(): void`: Forget held keys, presses, sticks and pointer movement (e.g. when a level loads).\n2322:- `get pointerLocked: boolean`\n2328:- `state(): InputState`: Held keys, queued presses and the pointer as data (`engine.snapshot()`), between frames.\n2335:- `setPointer(x: number, y: number, down?: boolean): void`: Test hook: put the pointer at (x, y) in normalised device coordinates, pressed or not.\n2338:- `get buttonEvents: readonly ButtonEvent[]`: This frame's pointer button presses and releases, in order, each with where the pointer was: a drag shorter than a frame (a script's) still starts where it started and ends where it ended. Recorded with the frame. UI that acts on clicks reads these; play read…\n2342:- `addPointer(dx: number, dy: number, wheel = 0): void`: Test hook: inject pointer movement / wheel for the next frame.\n2343:- `snapshot(dt: number, last?: SnapshotMemory): InputFrame`: This frame's input as data (after `beginFrame`), for a recording. `last` is the frame before: unchanged held keys, pointer and gamepad connection are left out.\n2345:- `playAfter(f: InputFrame): void`: Replay, after `beginFrame` (which polled no gamepads): sticks, pointer, wheel, gamepad connection.\n2350:Optional fields are left out when empty or zero; `held` and `pointer` also when unchanged","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_018H74VvCunqH3QRkJ8UxcC8","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
