{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FkaxAWH6GjCR2F4f59BoeD","type":"tool_result","content":"2462:### class AudioManager\n2463-\n2464-Web Audio for games: procedural retro sound effects (`SFX`, data), a small chiptune\n2465-sequencer (`Song`, data), optional audio files, and master / sfx / music volume + mute\n2466-persisted in localStorage. Available as `ctx.audio`.\n2467-\n2468-Browsers only allow sound after a user gesture, so the AudioContext is created on the\n2469-first key / pointer / touch input. Before that, and wherever Web Audio does not exist\n2470-(headless tests, old browsers), every call is a silent no-op that still records what\n2471-was played in `log`, so games behave identically and tests can assert on sounds.\n2472-\n2473-- `new AudioManager(target: EventTarget | null = typeof window !== 'undefined' ? window : null)`\n2474-- `static get supported: boolean`: Web Audio exists in this environment.\n2475-- `readonly sounds: Map<string, SoundDef>`: Sound registry: the built-in SFX plus anything registered or loaded.\n2476-- `readonly log: { name: string; at: number }[]`: The most recent plays (name and game-independent wall time), newest last; tooling/tests.\n2477-- `readonly counts: Record<string, number>`: How many times each sound was requested.\n2478-- `context: AudioContext | null`\n2479-- `get unlocked: boolean`: True once the AudioContext is running (after the first user input).\n2480-- `get volume: Readonly<AudioSettings>`: Current volumes and mute (persisted).\n2481-- `get muted: boolean`\n2482-- `get playing: string`: Name of the playing song ('' when none).\n2483-- `unlock(): void`: Create / resume the AudioContext. Called automatically on the first user input; call it yourself from a click handler if you start sound from your own UI.\n2484-- `register(name: string, def: SoundDef): void`: Add or replace a sound effect (data, see SoundDef).\n2485-- `play(sound: string | SoundDef, options: PlayOptions = {}): boolean`: Play a sound effect by name (built-in SFX, `register`ed or `load`ed) or directly from a SoundDef. Returns false when nothing could be heard (locked, muted, no Web Audio).\n2486-- `loop(sound: string | SoundDef, settings: VoiceSettings = {}): Voice`: Start a sound looping, as a voice you steer while it plays (volume, pan, muffle, pitch: with `spatialize` it sits at a place in the world). Before the first user input, or with no Web Audio, the voice keeps its settings silently and starts once audio unlocks.…\n2487-- `get loops: readonly Voice[]`: Voices playing or waiting to (tooling and tests).\n2488-- `stopLoops(): void`: Stop every looping voice (the engine does this when a level unloads).\n2489-- `load(name: string, url: string): Promise<void>`: Load an audio file (wav/ogg/mp3…) under `name`; `play(name)` then plays it. Works before the first user input too: the file is decoded once audio unlocks.\n2490-- `playMusic(song: Song | null, name = 'song'): void`: Start a song (looping by default), replacing the current one. `null` stops music.\n2491-- `stopMusic(): void`\n2492-- `persist: boolean`: Volume changes are written to storage. The engine turns this off while a replay plays: the recording sets the volumes it set, nothing is written, and the player's come back after.\n2493-- `setVolume(channel: VolumeChannel, value: number): void`\n2494-- `setMuted(muted: boolean): void`\n2495-- `toggleMute(): boolean`\n2496-- `resetVolumes(): void`: The default volumes, sound on (the settings panel's Reset).\n2497-- `update(): void`: Engine: once per rendered frame. Schedules the next notes of the song.\n2498-- `dispose(): void`: Stop everything and close the AudioContext.\n2499-\n2500-### interface AudioSettings\n2501-\n2502-- `master: number`\n2503-- `sfx: number`\n2504-- `music: number`\n2505-- `muted: boolean`\n2506-\n2507-### type Instrument\n2508-\n2509-```ts\n2510-type Instrument = Omit<SoundDef, 'freq' | 'freqEnd' | 'sustain' | 'delay'>\n2511-```\n2512-\n2513-A track's instrument: a SoundDef without pitch or length (each note sets those).\n2514-\n2515-### interface Listener\n2516-\n2517-- `position: V3Like`\n2518-- `right: V3Like`: The listener's right, in world space (unit): the camera's right for a third-person game.\n2519-\n2520-### muffleCutoff\n2521-\n2522-```ts\n2552:### interface PlayOptions\n2553-\n2554-- `volume?: number`: 0..1 multiplier on the sound's own volume.\n2555-- `pitch?: number`: Pitch shift in semitones (playback rate), e.g. a rising combo.\n2556-- `pan?: number`: Stereo position -1 (left) .. 1 (right).\n2557-\n2558-### renderSound()\n2559-\n2560-```ts\n2561-function renderSound(def: SoundDef, sampleRate = 44100, seed = 1): Float32Array<ArrayBuffer>\n2562-```\n2563-\n2564-Render a sound to mono samples in -1..1.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"75cb47e1-b6a0-4fd4-af20-38b42f9600a5","uuid":"d602bbe7-5e3c-4f20-85cf-4585507c2ee0","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:33:55.048Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"2462:### class AudioManager\n2463-\n2464-Web Audio for games: procedural retro sound effects (`SFX`, data), a small chiptune\n2465-sequencer (`Song`, data), optional audio files, and master / sfx / music volume + mute\n2466-persisted in localStorage. Available as `ctx.audio`.\n2467-\n2468-Browsers only allow sound after a user gesture, so the AudioContext is created on the\n2469-first key / pointer / touch input. Before that, and wherever Web Audio does not exist\n2470-(headless tests, old browsers), every call is a silent no-op that still records what\n2471-was played in `log`, so games behave identically and tests can assert on sounds.\n2472-\n2473-- `new AudioManager(target: EventTarget | null = typeof window !== 'undefined' ? window : null)`\n2474-- `static get supported: boolean`: Web Audio exists in this environment.\n2475-- `readonly sounds: Map<string, SoundDef>`: Sound registry: the built-in SFX plus anything registered or loaded.\n2476-- `readonly log: { name: string; at: number }[]`: The most recent plays (name and game-independent wall time), newest last; tooling/tests.\n2477-- `readonly counts: Record<string, number>`: How many times each sound was requested.\n2478-- `context: AudioContext | null`\n2479-- `get unlocked: boolean`: True once the AudioContext is running (after the first user input).\n2480-- `get volume: Readonly<AudioSettings>`: Current volumes and mute (persisted).\n2481-- `get muted: boolean`\n2482-- `get playing: string`: Name of the playing song ('' when none).\n2483-- `unlock(): void`: Create / resume the AudioContext. Called automatically on the first user input; call it yourself from a click handler if you start sound from your own UI.\n2484-- `register(name: string, def: SoundDef): void`: Add or replace a sound effect (data, see SoundDef).\n2485-- `play(sound: string | SoundDef, options: PlayOptions = {}): boolean`: Play a sound effect by name (built-in SFX, `register`ed or `load`ed) or directly from a SoundDef. Returns false when nothing could be heard (locked, muted, no Web Audio).\n2486-- `loop(sound: string | SoundDef, settings: VoiceSettings = {}): Voice`: Start a sound looping, as a voice you steer while it plays (volume, pan, muffle, pitch: with `spatialize` it sits at a place in the world). Before the first user input, or with no Web Audio, the voice keeps its settings silently and starts once audio unlocks.…\n2487-- `get loops: readonly Voice[]`: Voices playing or waiting to (tooling and tests).\n2488-- `stopLoops(): void`: Stop every looping voice (the engine does this when a level unloads).\n2489-- `load(name: string, url: string): Promise<void>`: Load an audio file (wav/ogg/mp3…) under `name`; `play(name)` then plays it. Works before the first user input too: the file is decoded once audio unlocks.\n2490-- `playMusic(song: Song | null, name = 'song'): void`: Start a song (looping by default), replacing the current one. `null` stops music.\n2491-- `stopMusic(): void`\n2492-- `persist: boolean`: Volume changes are written to storage. The engine turns this off while a replay plays: the recording sets the volumes it set, nothing is written, and the player's come back after.\n2493-- `setVolume(channel: VolumeChannel, value: number): void`\n2494-- `setMuted(muted: boolean): void`\n2495-- `toggleMute(): boolean`\n2496-- `resetVolumes(): void`: The default volumes, sound on (the settings panel's Reset).\n2497-- `update(): void`: Engine: once per rendered frame. Schedules the next notes of the song.\n2498-- `dispose(): void`: Stop everything and close the AudioContext.\n2499-\n2500-### interface AudioSettings\n2501-\n2502-- `master: number`\n2503-- `sfx: number`\n2504-- `music: number`\n2505-- `muted: boolean`\n2506-\n2507-### type Instrument\n2508-\n2509-```ts\n2510-type Instrument = Omit<SoundDef, 'freq' | 'freqEnd' | 'sustain' | 'delay'>\n2511-```\n2512-\n2513-A track's instrument: a SoundDef without pitch or length (each note sets those).\n2514-\n2515-### interface Listener\n2516-\n2517-- `position: V3Like`\n2518-- `right: V3Like`: The listener's right, in world space (unit): the camera's right for a third-person game.\n2519-\n2520-### muffleCutoff\n2521-\n2522-```ts\n2552:### interface PlayOptions\n2553-\n2554-- `volume?: number`: 0..1 multiplier on the sound's own volume.\n2555-- `pitch?: number`: Pitch shift in semitones (playback rate), e.g. a rising combo.\n2556-- `pan?: number`: Stereo position -1 (left) .. 1 (right).\n2557-\n2558-### renderSound()\n2559-\n2560-```ts\n2561-function renderSound(def: SoundDef, sampleRate = 44100, seed = 1): Float32Array<ArrayBuffer>\n2562-```\n2563-\n2564-Render a sound to mono samples in -1..1.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01FkaxAWH6GjCR2F4f59BoeD","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
