{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkhxZjgwsyB5EMyGdM6K","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The game is built and everything in the plan that can be done on this computer is done. The single deliverable is `TraumaCantina-TraumaCenterSecondOpinion-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261105-162024.html` (7.1 MB) in the work folder root. Beside it are `exit-interview.json` (checked: it parses), the dev folder `TraumaCantina-TraumaCenterSecondOpinion-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261105-162024/`, and `PROGRESS.md`.\n\nIt is **Trauma Cantina — Second Helpings**, picked at random (index 3 of 21). The full test command (`node tests/run.mjs`) passes 2502 of 2502 checks, including the browser checks and all 5 AI Hub harness scenarios.\n\n**What's in it**\n- **Campaign:** 10 operations, each with its story scene, patient chart and follow-up lines, plus the ending, the Shift Report and credits.\n- **Operating:** all eight instruments plus dressing, paddles and massage, vitals, clock and mistakes, ranks, both gifts (The Quiet and The Second Look), Code Blue, and the Intern/Resident/Attending difficulties.\n- **Bosses:** Introit, Lacrimosa, Dies Irae, and the three-stage Libera Me with a bot partner.\n- **Multiplayer:** Consult couch co-op for 1–4 seats, and AI Hub shared-world sessions with the game's own card.\n- **Shell:** title, menus, Settings, Pause with Dev Mode (live balance sliders with reset), attract mode after 10 s idle, the touch-only message, and the About/Credits pages.\n- **Sound and look:** all music, sound effects and gibberish voices are written in code, with music at 10% by default. The engine file is unmodified.\n- **Docs and bot:** the bot plays attract mode, the test playthrough, the balance report and the Op 9 partner. `docs/AUTHORING.md` explains how to add content.\n\n**Where I deviated or skipped**\n- The comm-strip portrait is a pixel-art face, not the 3D bust; story scenes do use real 3D busts.\n- I skipped the optional live monitor and mirror touches from the plan's cut list.\n- The models are built from primitives in code, not the engine's `model()` format, so the `check.mjs --sheets` step doesn't apply.\n- On a 342-pixel-wide window the comm strip shows three lines instead of two, because 60-character lines can't fit that width.\n- Several screens were only spot-checked on screenshots at 960×540, and a few at 1920×1080.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-05 16:20:24\n- **Source:** Trauma Center: Second Opinion (Atlus, Wii, 2006); an original game inspired by it\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Simulation (surgical action with visual-novel drama); first-person surgeon's-eye fixed close-up on a 3D field, with close-ups and wide shots in story scenes\n- **Tech:** Riftlight Pixel Engine 0.46.0 (three.js r186 WebGPU, Rapier), plain JavaScript modules, esbuild 0.28 single-file bundle, AI Hub session client 1.4.0 (protocol 1), Playwright 1.63 for tests\n- **Art Direction:** engine-native low-poly 3D rendered as pixel art; tissue painted at runtime on a dithered canvas; busts, hands, tools and figures built in code; Kenney furniture props recoloured\n- **Animation:** engine animation clips on custom rigged figures, plus procedural tool, bust and tissue animation\n- **Audio:** all music, effects and gibberish voices written in code; no audio files; music defaults to 10%\n- **Online:** AI Hub session protocol v1, shared-world, 1–4 seats; none outside a session; couch co-op on one screen\n- **Testing:** headless Node tests of the sim, content lint, whole-campaign bot playthrough, balance report, Chromium browser checks, and the AI Hub harness; no subagents\n- **Research:** the plan's planner read the source's Wikipedia page, the hub's protocol and the engine kit and ran engine spikes; this build read the plan, the engine guide and the hub README and spiked canvas textures, kit packs and rig-compatible figures\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** added on import\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** about 16 (the counts are my estimate, not a log). They included an unfinishable Dies Irae final cut, stale bot targets, a magnet snap loop, a pause menu that closed itself, a hub card crash, a headless crash and overflowing comm text.\n- **Critical / game-breaking:** 4 — the Dies Irae final cut, the pause menu, the hub card crash, and a lifted-plate trap.\n- **Most helpful test:** the scripted bot playthrough of every operation and the whole campaign in Node. It found sim bugs in seconds and also served as the balance report.\n- **Least helpful test:** the first blank-canvas screenshots, and the pixel-width text lint, which only approximates the font.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the look pipeline, plus headless mode and the check tool.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** a game needs a `cameraTarget` hook or start fails; the HUD has no alpha rectangle; HUD text takes number colours but not hex strings.\n- **Most important thing built myself:** the pure-data surgery sim (tools, strains, bot, rewind), the tissue painter, the menu and prompt toolkit, and the gibberish voices.\n- **Hardest part:** keeping gameplay in the fixed step while the UI reads input in `update`, and getting 3D busts into the HUD strip.\n- **Changed in the engine:** none.\n- **One change:** HUD rects and text with alpha and wrapping, and a render-to-HUD helper for 3D portraits.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the plan's verified facts, exact numbers, build order and cut list made a huge scope tractable.\n- **Confusing:** 60-character lines versus a 342-pixel-wide HUD can't both hold, and the plan asks for 3D busts in the comm strip, which the HUD can't draw.\n- **Hardest thing:** fitting ten operations, five bosses, co-op, the hub, the bot and the whole shell into one medium-effort run without stubs.\n- **Would change:** say which plan details are hard requirements, give a smaller minimum scope, and fix the line-width rule."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":757,"cache_read_input_tokens":504689,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":757},"output_tokens":795,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"75cb47e1-b6a0-4fd4-af20-38b42f9600a5","uuid":"f7ba5a22-89d4-4e25-a885-45a5ba09a7a3","timestamp":"2026-11-06T00:12:46.071Z","request_id":"req_011CgkhxZSb9nQ6F1SFePByh"}
