{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011c5xX7orLaDxA16SbFX6Th","type":"tool_result","content":"4627:### class RenderView\n4628-\n4629-- `new RenderView(o: RenderViewOptions = {})`\n4630-- `static screen(object: Object3D): void`: Put `object` (and its children) on the screens' layer.\n4631-- `readonly target: RenderTarget`\n4632-- `readonly camera: PerspectiveCamera`\n4633-- `every: number`: Render every nth frame.\n4634-- `renders: number`: Times it has rendered.\n4635-- `enabled: boolean`\n4636-- `get texture: Texture`\n4637-- `setSize(w: number, h: number): void`: Resize the texture (the camera's aspect follows).\n4638-- `render(renderer: WebGPURenderer, scene: Scene): boolean`: Draw `scene` from the view's camera into its texture, if this is one of its frames. True if it drew.\n4639-- `attach(view: View, scene: Scene): () => void`: Render before every frame of `view` (`engine.renderer`). Returns a stop. Headless the hook is kept and never runs.\n4640-- `screenMaterial(): MeshBasicNodeMaterial`: An unlit material showing the view (a new one each call: tint it as you like).\n4641-- `dispose(): void`\n4642-\n4643-### interface RenderViewOptions\n4644-\n4645-- `size?: readonly [number, number]`: Texture size in pixels (default [160, 90]).\n4646-- `fov?: number`: Vertical field of view, degrees (default 60).\n4647-- `near?: number`\n4648-- `far?: number`\n4649-- `every?: number`: Render every nth frame (default 1): a slow refresh costs less.\n4469:### class Mirror\n4470-\n4471-- `new Mirror(o: MirrorOptions = {})`\n4472-- `readonly mesh: Mesh`\n4473-- `readonly target: RenderTarget`\n4474-- `enabled: boolean`: False: the glass shows plain glass and nothing is rendered for it.\n4475-- `renders: number`: Times it has rendered.\n4476-- `render(renderer: WebGPURenderer, scene: Scene, camera: Camera, width: number, height: number): boolean`: Reflect `camera` in the glass and draw `scene` from there into the texture (sized `width` x `height`, the art resolution). Skipped when the camera \n4477-- `attach(view: View, scene: Scene): () => void`: Render before every frame of `view` (`engine.renderer`), from its camera, at its art size. Returns a stop. Headless the hook is kept and never runs (nothing is drawn).\n4478-- `dispose(): void`\n4479-\n4480-### interface MirrorOptions\n4481-\n4482-- `size?: readonly [number, number]`: Width and height of the glass (m). Default [4, 2].\n4483-- `tint?: number`: A colour the reflection leans toward, and how much (0..1). Default a faint blue, 0.15.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"75cb47e1-b6a0-4fd4-af20-38b42f9600a5","uuid":"81703c2e-0dc7-404e-a062-a0958500c911","timestamp":"2026-11-06T00:13:13.558Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"4627:### class RenderView\n4628-\n4629-- `new RenderView(o: RenderViewOptions = {})`\n4630-- `static screen(object: Object3D): void`: Put `object` (and its children) on the screens' layer.\n4631-- `readonly target: RenderTarget`\n4632-- `readonly camera: PerspectiveCamera`\n4633-- `every: number`: Render every nth frame.\n4634-- `renders: number`: Times it has rendered.\n4635-- `enabled: boolean`\n4636-- `get texture: Texture`\n4637-- `setSize(w: number, h: number): void`: Resize the texture (the camera's aspect follows).\n4638-- `render(renderer: WebGPURenderer, scene: Scene): boolean`: Draw `scene` from the view's camera into its texture, if this is one of its frames. True if it drew.\n4639-- `attach(view: View, scene: Scene): () => void`: Render before every frame of `view` (`engine.renderer`). Returns a stop. Headless the hook is kept and never runs.\n4640-- `screenMaterial(): MeshBasicNodeMaterial`: An unlit material showing the view (a new one each call: tint it as you like).\n4641-- `dispose(): void`\n4642-\n4643-### interface RenderViewOptions\n4644-\n4645-- `size?: readonly [number, number]`: Texture size in pixels (default [160, 90]).\n4646-- `fov?: number`: Vertical field of view, degrees (default 60).\n4647-- `near?: number`\n4648-- `far?: number`\n4649-- `every?: number`: Render every nth frame (default 1): a slow refresh costs less.\n4469:### class Mirror\n4470-\n4471-- `new Mirror(o: MirrorOptions = {})`\n4472-- `readonly mesh: Mesh`\n4473-- `readonly target: RenderTarget`\n4474-- `enabled: boolean`: False: the glass shows plain glass and nothing is rendered for it.\n4475-- `renders: number`: Times it has rendered.\n4476-- `render(renderer: WebGPURenderer, scene: Scene, camera: Camera, width: number, height: number): boolean`: Reflect `camera` in the glass and draw `scene` from there into the texture (sized `width` x `height`, the art resolution). Skipped when the camera \n4477-- `attach(view: View, scene: Scene): () => void`: Render before every frame of `view` (`engine.renderer`), from its camera, at its art size. Returns a stop. Headless the hook is kept and never runs (nothing is drawn).\n4478-- `dispose(): void`\n4479-\n4480-### interface MirrorOptions\n4481-\n4482-- `size?: readonly [number, number]`: Width and height of the glass (m). Default [4, 2].\n4483-- `tint?: number`: A colour the reflection leans toward, and how much (0..1). Default a faint blue, 0.15.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_011c5xX7orLaDxA16SbFX6Th","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
