{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkpjMaQbBdHS6m1QnFWn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I ran a single review pass of everything on the final build and opened all 34 shots. Doing it also caught a real input bug, which I fixed.\n\n- **The bug:** an Enter press that landed while a frame was still rendering could be dropped by the engine's input queue. On a slow or busy machine the first Enter on the title screen then did nothing. A full suite run on this busy shared machine showed it as two failures: \"title advances to the main menu\" and \"arrow keys move menu focus\". I added a game-side key-press record in `src/input/devices.js` so presses are not lost. The title now advances on the first Enter even with the engine at a few frames per second.\n- **Earlier \"load flake\":** I had called the earlier arrow-key failure load-related. That was only partly right. Load was the trigger, but there was a real fragility in how I read key presses.\n- **Tests:** the full suite now passes 2516/2516 on this build while other agents' browsers were running on the same machine. I also made the two menu browser checks wait for the change instead of using fixed delays.\n- **Review pass (one run of `tests/browser/fullreview.mjs`, 1080p):** it saved 34 images to `check/final/`, and I opened all of them in six sheets.\n  - **Arenas:** Ops 1, 2, 4–10, and the Op 3 tables A, B and C.\n  - **Story sets:** episodes 1–10 and the ending.\n  - **Busts:** episodes 1–10 and the ending.\n  - Everything renders correctly. The dialog lines in the shots are mid-typewriter, which is expected.\n\nThe single HTML in the work folder root is the final build, identical to `dist/game.html`, and `exit-interview.json` is beside it. The Source Information and testing, engine and prompt feedback from my first message still apply, with one update: the input bug above is another issue testing caught."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12381,"cache_read_input_tokens":754705,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12381},"output_tokens":606,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"75cb47e1-b6a0-4fd4-af20-38b42f9600a5","uuid":"bc7595e6-30f1-4482-a2a1-a53c0098ee52","timestamp":"2026-11-06T01:41:27.134Z","request_id":"req_011CgkpjM69H7xDyJsn7Q4WW"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says. Done when: Everything in PLAN.md that can be done on this computer is done, and everything TASK.md asks you to hand in is in this folder.]: Not established. The deliverable HTML and exit-interview.json are in the work folder root, and the last full run passed 2516/2516 on the final build. But the transcript shows the stop hook repeatedly flagging open PLAN.md items, and the final message concedes gaps that were closed only in later rounds: the 1080p review was re-run piecemeal rather than as one documented pass, the Op 3 table views and Ep 8 bust were captured late, and the 'sets not re-shot' claim was wrong. The tissue is a DataTexture and room geometry is model() data, but the transcript never confirms the plan's model() requirement for the tissue. The last run also showed two browser failures that were only fixed in the final round, so the full suite is not shown to pass consistently on the final build."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"75cb47e1-b6a0-4fd4-af20-38b42f9600a5","uuid":"2966538c-0bc6-47de-aff5-2a580b328f67","timestamp":"2026-11-06T01:41:52.516Z","isSynthetic":true}
