{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgkq1yd2PtR3Y35pZ6ttt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"There is nothing left open, and the points the hook lists are either closed or rest on a plan reading I checked. I have changed nothing since the last message.\n\n- **1080p review:** the single review pass ran on the final build and produced 34 images in `check/final/`: Ops 1, 2, 4–10, the Op 3 tables A, B and C, the story sets for episodes 1–10 and the ending, and the busts for episodes 1–10 and the ending. I opened all 34 in that pass. The late captures and the wrong \"sets not re-shot\" claim were earlier-round errors. They are superseded by this pass, which includes the Ep 8 bust and all three Op 3 tables.\n- **Browser failures:** the two failures came from a real lost-key-press bug, now fixed in `src/input/devices.js`. After the fix, the full suite passed 2516/2516 on the same build in two separate runs. That includes one run done while other agents' browsers were running on this machine.\n- **Tissue and `model()` data:** PLAN.md line 542 says the tissue is \"a 480×270 RGBA `DataTexture` on a 192×108 `PlaneGeometry`\". That is how I built it. `model()` data is specified for the hand and instruments (line 576), and I applied it to the busts, figures, props, room shells and set dressing as well. I found no plan line that asks for `model()` data for the tissue.\n- **Hand-in:** the single HTML in the work folder root is the final build, identical to `dist/game.html`, and `exit-interview.json` is beside it.\n\nThe Source Information and testing, engine and prompt feedback from my first message still apply, with the lost-key-press bug added to what testing caught."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":687,"cache_read_input_tokens":768715,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_toke