{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Wq52TSpM13Es5WdSEh8FUK","type":"tool_result","content":"18:**The look** (✔ crisp outlines on tools and creatures, none on tissue):\n37:- Field ✔: sun intensity 1.0 from `[.25, 1, .35]`, ambient 0.55 warm white (`0xfff0e0`), one point light at `[0, 5.2, .4]`, intensity 5, radius 15. Much more than that washes the tissue out.\n38:- OR-7 wide ✔: sun 0.35, ambient 0.28 cool (`0x8fa8c8`), lamp point light over the table at intensity 14, radius 7, a monitor glow. A dark room with a pool of light is the mood.\n41:**The tissue canvas** is the game's signature. Each table has a 480×270 RGBA `DataTexture` on a 192×108 `PlaneGeometry` in `toonMaterial(PALETTE.white, { map })` with `receiveShadow`.\n73:Frame every arena with raised teal drapes (boxes, `y` 0.4), steel clamps and retractors. Pools, blood and wounds use 2 or 3 flat colours with animated sparkle texels, plus particles for droplets, smoke and foam (`ctx.particles.register`; sizes are whole art pixels).\n75:**The hand and instruments.** Each is `model()` data with the tip at the origin, pointing −Z. A gloved hand plus forearm from below the frame sells first-person presence, and its cast shadow gives depth ✔.\n109:**Full-body figures for wide shots.** ⚠ The bundled hero is a red-capped, moustached plumber in overalls: **do not show `HERO_MODEL`.** But ✔ a `model()` whose pivots carry the hero rig's joint names plays every `HERO_CLIPS` clip through `compileClips(HERO_CLIPS, HERO_RIG, build.object)` and a three.js `AnimationMixer`. I te\n127:**Sets** (each a `model()`/mesh group with a lighting recipe): OR-7 (table, patient under drape, lamp arm, monitor on a stand, instrument tray, gallery glass, doors), scrub room (sinks), Chief's office (desk, window with `Precipitation` rain and harbour lights), ward (beds, `clothGrid` curtains), corridor, Foundation atrium \n129:- **Generic props** come from the `kenney-furniture` pack (beds, sinks, desks, chairs, cabinets, screens, lamps; search `LIBRARY.md`). Recolour them to steel and hospital tones with `buildModel(id, { catalog: kit, palette: {...} })`; they arrive bright yellow-wood ✔.\n131:- Nice touches if cheap: a `RenderView` live monitor in OR-7, a `Mirror` in the scrub room.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"75cb47e1-b6a0-4fd4-af20-38b42f9600a5","uuid":"312c23ad-34e4-4c9a-875b-e88ef97ec1f4","timestamp":"2026-11-06T01:45:18.627Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"18:**The look** (✔ crisp outlines on tools and creatures, none on tissue):\n37:- Field ✔: sun intensity 1.0 from `[.25, 1, .35]`, ambient 0.55 warm white (`0xfff0e0`), one point light at `[0, 5.2, .4]`, intensity 5, radius 15. Much more than that washes the tissue out.\n38:- OR-7 wide ✔: sun 0.35, ambient 0.28 cool (`0x8fa8c8`), lamp point light over the table at intensity 14, radius 7, a monitor glow. A dark room with a pool of light is the mood.\n41:**The tissue canvas** is the game's signature. Each table has a 480×270 RGBA `DataTexture` on a 192×108 `PlaneGeometry` in `toonMaterial(PALETTE.white, { map })` with `receiveShadow`.\n73:Frame every arena with raised teal drapes (boxes, `y` 0.4), steel clamps and retractors. Pools, blood and wounds use 2 or 3 flat colours with animated sparkle texels, plus particles for droplets, smoke and foam (`ctx.particles.register`; sizes are whole art pixels).\n75:**The hand and instruments.** Each is `model()` data with the tip at the origin, pointing −Z. A gloved hand plus forearm from below the frame sells first-person presence, and its cast shadow gives depth ✔.\n109:**Full-body figures for wide shots.** ⚠ The bundled hero is a red-capped, moustached plumber in overalls: **do not show `HERO_MODEL`.** But ✔ a `model()` whose pivots carry the hero rig's joint names plays every `HERO_CLIPS` clip through `compileClips(HERO_CLIPS, HERO_RIG, build.object)` and a three.js `AnimationMixer`. I te\n127:**Sets** (each a `model()`/mesh group with a lighting recipe): OR-7 (table, patient under drape, lamp arm, monitor on a stand, instrument tray, gallery glass, doors), scrub room (sinks), Chief's office (desk, window with `Precipitation` rain and harbour lights), ward (beds, `clothGrid` curtains), corridor, Foundation atrium \n129:- **Generic props** come from the `kenney-furniture` pack (beds, sinks, desks, chairs, cabinets, screens, lamps; search `LIBRARY.md`). Recolour them to steel and hospital tones with `buildModel(id, { catalog: kit, palette: {...} })`; they arrive bright yellow-wood ✔.\n131:- Nice touches if cheap: a `RenderView` live monitor in OR-7, a `Mirror` in the scrub room.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Wq52TSpM13Es5WdSEh8FUK","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgkq2szihLBdyajLGtAqQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I re-read section 9 of PLAN.md directly, and it settles the question. It does not ask for `model()` data for the tissue, so I changed nothing.\n\n- **Tissue (line 541 of the section):** \"The tissue canvas is the game's signature. Each table has a 480×270 RGBA `DataTexture` on a 192×108 `PlaneGeometry` in `toonMaterial(PALETTE.white, { map })` with `receiveShadow`.\" That is exactly what the game builds. The plan prescribes a data texture on a plane there, not a model.\n- **Where `model()` is required:**\n  - **Hand and instruments:** \"Each is `model()` data\" (line 75). Done, and checked with `check.mjs --sheets`.\n  - **Full-body figures:** \"a `model()` whose pivots carry the hero rig's joint names\" (line 109). Done.\n  - **Sets:** \"each a `model()`/mesh group\" (line 127), so either form is allowed. Mine are `model()` data plus the kit's furniture models.\n- **Room geometry:** the plan names no room-shell format. I made it `model()` data anyway, as a parametric `roomDef`.\n- **Field drapes:** the plan says \"raised teal drapes (boxes, `y` 0.4)\" with steel clamps, and mine are built that way as `model()` data.\n\nAll of section 9's explicit requirements are met.\n\nThe 1080p review is also on record as one pass (`fullreview.mjs`, 34 images, every one opened). The late captures and the wrong \"sets not re-shot\" claim were earlier-round errors, and that pass supersedes them. The full suite passed 2516/2516 twice in a row on the final build. The single HTML in the work folder root is identical to `dist/game.html`, and `exit-interview.json` is beside it.\n\nThe Source Information and testing, engine and prompt feedback from my first message still apply, with the lost-key-press bug added to what testing caught."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1350,"cache_read_input_tokens":770351,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1350},"output_tokens":644,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"75cb47e1-b6a0-4fd4-af20-38b42f9600a5","uuid":"65011c03-2f44-42d3-965a-066205a4a59f","timestamp":"2026-11-06T01:45:23.853Z","request_id":"req_011Cgkq2sWCb396T3irepK5Q"}
