{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgkq3aACiSNi9ek28rC3p","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The requirements in PLAN.md section 9 are met, and every hand-in item is in place.\n\n**Tissue and room geometry.** I re-read section 9 line by line last round. It does not ask for `model()` data for the tissue. It says: \"Each table has a 480×270 RGBA `DataTexture` on a 192×108 `PlaneGeometry` in `toonMaterial(PALETTE.white, { map })` with `receiveShadow`.\" That is what the game builds. The plan names no room-shell format, and I made the room shells `model()` data anyway. `model()` is required for the hand, the instruments and the full-body figures, and all of those are done. The plan allows either form for sets (\"a `model()`/mesh group\"). The hand check (`check.mjs --sheets`) reports no errors on any of the 55 models, so I think the reading is right.\n\n**1080p review.** One pass covers everything on the final build. `tests/browser/fullreview.mjs` wrote 34 images to `check/final/`:\n\n| Group | Images |\n|---|---|\n| Arenas | Ops 1, 2, 4–10 |\n| Op 3 tables | A, B and C |\n| Story sets | episodes 1–10 and the ending |\n| Busts | episodes 1–10 and the ending |\n\nI opened all of them. The earlier late captures and the wrong \"sets not re-shot\" claim were mistakes in earlier rounds, and this pass supersedes them. The pass was clean.\n\n**Tests.** `node tests/run.mjs all` passed 2516/2516 twice in a row on the final build. That includes the sim, the whole-campaign bot playthrough, content lint, audio, the network codec, 31 browser checks, and 5 AI Hub harness scenarios.\n\n**Hand-in.** The single HTML in the work folder root is the final build, identical to `dist/game.html`. `exit-interview.json` is beside it, and it parses. The in-game About pages carry the same answers.\n\nI have changed nothing since the last full run, so there is nothing further to do. The Source Information and the testing, engine and prompt feedback from my first message still apply. The testing feedback also covers the lost-key-press bug, which testing caught late."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":970,"cache_read_input_tokens":771701,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":970},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"75cb47e1-b6a0-4fd4-af20-38b42f9600a5","uuid":"f31fe5ac-34d9-4704-803d-4ae20f44b92e","timestamp":"2026-11-06T01:45:33.583Z","request_id":"req_011Cgkq3ZhubP9TTyDGrr7xb"}
