{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgkq6WuZftSayekyn3YJ8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have nothing new to do, and nothing has changed in the work since the last run.\n\nThe one disputed point is whether PLAN.md asks for `model()` data for the tissue. I checked the plan text directly, and it does not. I printed the relevant lines from the file in my last few messages. Line 542 describes the tissue as \"a 480×270 RGBA `DataTexture` on a 192×108 `PlaneGeometry`\", which is how it is built. The plan asks for `model()` data for the hand and instruments (line 576) and for the full-body figures (line 610), and both are `model()` data. Sets may be \"a `model()`/mesh group\", and mine are `model()` data. The room shells are `model()` data too, which the plan does not require.\n\nThe earlier late or wrong review claims were errors from earlier rounds. One later pass covers everything on the final build:\n- It produced 34 images in `check/final/`: the arenas, the Op 3 tables, the story sets and the busts. I opened every one of them.\n- `node tests/run.mjs all` passed 2516/2516 twice in a row on the final build.\n- The single HTML in the work folder root is identical to `dist/game.html`.\n- `exit-interview.json` is beside it and parses.\n\nI'm not making further changes. The Source Information and testing, engine and prompt feedback from my first message still apply."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":816,"cache_read_input_tokens":775848,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":816},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"75cb47e1-b6a0-4fd4-af20-38b42f9600a5","uuid":"fa2955cc-a337-4e8c-a760-12e1635deca9","